    return $value > 2; // 明确的过滤条件
});
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule requires strict type checking for the usage of the `array_filter` function.

##### Rule Significance
When using `array_filter`, it is recommended to pass a callback function to ensure that the process of filtering the array is explicit and type-safe. Not using it strictly may lead to unexpected results.

##### Incorrect Example
```php
$arr = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
$result = array_filter($arr); // The absence of a callback function may cause an error
```

##### Correct Example
```php
$arr = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
$result = array_filter($arr, function($value) {
    return $value > 2; // Explicit filtering condition
});
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在代码中使用断言时，如果类型已经被缩小，可能会导致误解或错误执行。

##### 规则意义
该规则确保在使用断言（如`assert()`）时，前面的条件已经明确地缩小了变量的类型。若未能这样做，可能会导致后续代码不能正确处理变量类型，增加出错的风险。

##### 错误示例
```php
function processValue(?int $value) {
    assert($value !== null);
    // 这里假设$value已经不是null，但实际上，
    // 编译器无法确定$value的确切类型
    echo $value * 2; // 可能导致错误，若$value是null
}
```

##### 正确示例
```php
function processValue(?int $value) {
    assert($value !== null);
    if ($value !== null) {
        echo $value * 2; // 现在可以安全使用$value，因为我们已经确认它不是null
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
Using assertions in code can lead to misunderstandings or erroneous execution if the type has already been narrowed.

##### Rule Meaning
This rule ensures that when using assertions (such as `assert()`), the preceding conditions have clearly narrowed down the type of the variable. Failing to do so may result in subsequent code not correctly handling the variable's type, increasing the risk of errors.

##### Error Example
```php
function processValue(?int $value) {
    assert($value !== null);
    // Here it is assumed that $value is no longer null, but in reality,
    // the compiler cannot determine the exact type of $value
    echo $value * 2; // May cause an error if $value is null
}
```

##### Correct Example
```php
function processValue(?int $value) {
    assert($value !== null);
    if ($value !== null) {
        echo $value * 2; // Now it is safe to use $value, as we have confirmed it is not null
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则旨在确保在使用 traits 时，所有断言方法均在测试代码中合理使用。使用 traits 中的断言方法可能导致代码可用性和可读性降低。

##### 规则意义
确保在使用 traits 中定义的断言方法时，遵循最佳实践，避免不必要的复杂性和潜在的代码缺陷。

##### 错误示例
'''php
trait ExampleTrait {
    public function assertSomething() {
        // 示例代码
    }
}
class ExampleTest {
    use ExampleTrait;
    public function testExample() {
        // 错误：直接调用 trait 中的断言
        $this->assertSomething();
    }
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
trait ExampleTrait {
    public function assertSomething() {
        // 示例代码
    }
}
class ExampleTest {
    protected function assertSomething() {
        // 正确：在测试类中定义断言
        $this->assertSame(
            expectedValue,
            $actualValue
        );
    }
    public function testExample() {
        $this->assertSomething();
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule aims to ensure that all assertion methods are reasonably used in test code when using traits. Using assertion methods from traits may lead to reduced code usability and readability.

##### Rule Significance
Ensure that best practices are followed when using assertion methods defined in traits to avoid unnecessary complexity and potential code defects.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
trait ExampleTrait {
    public function assertSomething() {
        // 示例代码
    }
}
class ExampleTest {
    use ExampleTrait;
    public function testExample() {
        // 错误：直接调用 trait 中的断言
        $this->assertSomething();
    }
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
trait ExampleTrait {
    public function assertSomething() {
        // 示例代码
    }
}
class ExampleTest {
    protected function assertSomething() {
        // 正确：在测试类中定义断言
        $this->assertSame(
            expectedValue,
            $actualValue
        );
    }
    public function testExample() {
        $this->assertSomething();
    }
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在使用类型断言时，若类型无法确定而导致的错误将会影响代码的健壮性和可维护性。

##### 规则意义
此规则提醒开发者避免在上下文不明确或无法解析的情况下使用类型断言，以防止运行时错误和类型安全问题。

##### 错误示例
'''php
function processInput($input) {
    assert($input instanceof SomeClass);
    $input->doSomething();
}

processInput($value); // $value 类型不明确，会导致错误
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
function processInput($input) {
    if ($input instanceof SomeClass) {
        $input->doSomething();
    } else {
        throw new InvalidArgumentException('Input must be an instance of SomeClass');
    }
}

processInput($value); // 处理类型不正确的情况
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
When using type assertions, errors caused by undetermined types can affect the robustness and maintainability of the code.

##### Rule Significance
This rule reminds developers to avoid using type assertions in contexts that are unclear or unresolvable, in order to prevent runtime errors and type safety issues.

##### Error Example
'''php
function processInput($input) {
    assert($input instanceof SomeClass);
    $input->doSomething();
}

processInput($value); // $value type is unclear, which will cause an error
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
function processInput($input) {
    if ($input instanceof SomeClass) {
        $input->doSomething();
    } else {
        throw new InvalidArgumentException('Input must be an instance of SomeClass');
    }
}

processInput($value); // Handle cases with incorrect type
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则检查是否直接对类的私有属性进行赋值，这种做法被认为是不良实践。

##### 规则意义
私有属性应当通过公共方法进行访问和修改，直接赋值可能导致对象的状态不一致，并降低代码的可维护性和可读性。

##### 错误示例
```php
class Example {
    private $value;

    public function setValue($value) {
        $this->value = $value;
    }
}

$obj = new Example();
$obj->value = 5; // 错误：直接访问私有属性
```

##### 正确示例
```php
class Example {
    private $value;

    public function setValue($value) {
        $this->value = $value;
    }
}

$obj = new Example();
$obj->setValue(5); // 正确：通过公共方法设置私有属性
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule checks whether there is a direct assignment to a class's private properties, a practice considered poor.

##### Rule Significance
Private properties should be accessed and modified through public methods, as direct assignment may lead to inconsistent object states and reduce code maintainability and readability.

##### Incorrect Example
```php
class Example {
    private $value;

    public function setValue($value) {
        $this->value = $value;
    }
}

$obj = new Example();
$obj->value = 5; // Error: Direct access to private property
```

##### Correct Example
```php
class Example {
    private $value;

    public function setValue($value) {
        $this->value = $value;
    }
}

$obj = new Example();
$obj->setValue(5); // Correct: Setting private property through public method
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则检查是否在类的保护属性上直接进行赋值操作。

##### 规则意义
直接赋值可能会导致潜在的可访问性问题，继而影响代码的可维护性和可读性，尤其是在面向对象编程中。使用方法设置保护属性是更安全的做法。

##### 错误示例
```php
class User {
    protected $name;

    public function setName($name) {
        $this->name = $name; // 错误示例: 直接赋值给保护属性
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```php
class User {
    protected $name;

    public function setName($name) {
        // 正确的赋值方式，通过 setter 方法设置保护属性
        $this->name = $name;
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule checks for direct assignment operations on the protected properties of a class.

##### Rule Meaning
Direct assignments may lead to potential accessibility issues, which can affect the maintainability and readability of the code, especially in object-oriented programming. Using methods to set protected properties is a safer practice.

##### Incorrect Example
```php
class User {
    protected $name;

    public function setName($name) {
        $this->name = $name; // Incorrect Example: Direct assignment to a protected property
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```php
class User {
    protected $name;

    public function setName($name) {
        // Correct assignment method, setting protected property through setter method
        $this->name = $name;
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则用于检测对只读属性的赋值操作，确保不对只读属性进行直接赋值，以避免不必要的错误和潜在的代码缺陷。

##### 规则意义
只读属性通常在类中定义为只可读，对其进行直接赋值会导致代码逻辑错误，可能使类的状态不一致，进而引发难以发现的bug。

##### 错误示例
'''php
class User {
    private $name;
    private $age;

    public function __construct(string $name, int $age) {
        $this->name = $name;
        $this->age = $age;
    }

    public function getName(): string {
        return $this->name;
    }

    public function getAge(): int {
        return $this->age;
    }
}

$user = new User('Alice', 30);
$user->name = 'Bob'; // 错误：尝试修改只读属性
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
class User {
    private $name;
    private $age;

    public function __construct(string $name, int $age) {
        $this->name = $name;
        $this->age = $age;
    }

    public function getName(): string {
        return $this->name;
    }

    public function getAge(): int {
        return $this->age;
    }
}

$user = new User('Alice', 30);
// 正确用法：通过构造方法初始化只读属性
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is used to detect assignments to read-only properties, ensuring that direct assignments to read-only properties are avoided to prevent unnecessary errors and potential code defects.

##### Rule Significance
Read-only properties are typically defined in classes as read-only. Direct assignments to them can lead to logical errors in the code, possibly making the state of the class inconsistent, which can result in hard-to-detect bugs.

##### Erroneous Example
'''php
class User {
    private $name;
    private $age;

    public function __construct(string $name, int $age) {
        $this->name = $name;
        $this->age = $age;
    }

    public function getName(): string {
        return $this->name;
    }

    public function getAge(): int {
        return $this->age;
    }
}

$user = new User('Alice', 30);
$user->name = 'Bob'; // Error: Attempting to modify a read-only property
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
class User {
    private $name;
    private $age;

    public function __construct(string $name, int $age) {
        $this->name = $name;
        $this->age = $age;
    }

    public function getName(): string {
        return $this->name;
    }

    public function getAge(): int {
        return $this->age;
    }
}

$user = new User('Alice', 30);
// Correct usage: Initializing read-only properties through the constructor
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
本规则用于检查对象属性的类型分配，确保在类中定义的属性和通过构造函数或方法分配的值的类型一致。

##### 规则意义
确保属性的类型与分配给它们的值的类型相匹配，有助于避免运行时错误，并提高代码的可读性和可维护性。

