This rule is used to check the type assignment of object properties, ensuring that the types of the properties defined in the class are consistent with the types of values assigned through the constructor or methods.

##### Rule Significance
Ensuring that the types of properties match the types of the values assigned to them helps to avoid runtime errors and improves the readability and maintainability of the code.

