rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则用于检测对只读属性的赋值操作。

##### 规则意义
只读属性旨在保护数据的完整性，不允许被外部代码修改。如果代码尝试对只读属性进行赋值，将导致程序逻辑错误以及潜在的不可预期行为。

##### 错误示例
'''php
class User {
    private $name;
    private readonly $email;

    public function __construct($name, $email) {
        $this->name = $name;
        $this->email = $email;
    }

    public function updateEmail($newEmail) {
        // 错误示例：尝试修改只读属性
        $this->email = $newEmail; // 此行将导致静态分析警告
    }
}
'''  

##### 正确示例
'''php
class User {
    private $name;
    private readonly $email;

    public function __construct($name, $email) {
        $this->name = $name;
        $this->email = $email;
    }

    // 正确方式：只读属性不能被修改
    public function getEmail() {
        return $this->email;
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is used to detect assignment operations to read-only properties.

##### Rule Meaning
Read-only properties are designed to protect the integrity of data and are not allowed to be modified by external code. If the code attempts to assign a value to a read-only property, it will result in program logic errors and potential unexpected behavior.

##### Error Example
'''php
class User {
    private $name;
    private readonly $email;

    public function __construct($name, $email) {
        $this->name = $name;
        $this->email = $email;
    }

    public function updateEmail($newEmail) {
        // Error example: attempting to modify a read-only property
        $this->email = $newEmail; // This line will cause a static analysis warning
    }
}
'''  

##### Correct Example
'''php
class User {
    private $name;
    private readonly $email;

    public function __construct($name, $email) {
        $this->name = $name;
        $this->email = $email;
    }

    // Correct way: read-only properties cannot be modified
    public function getEmail() {
        return $this->email;
    }
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则检测在只读属性上执行赋值操作的情况，这通常是一个逻辑错误。

##### 规则意义
在面向对象编程中，声明为只读的属性通常不应被外部修改。如果尝试在这样的属性上进行赋值，将可能导致意想不到的行为，从而影响代码的稳定性和可维护性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
class MyClass {
    /** @var string */
    private readonly string $readOnlyProperty;

    public function __construct(string $value) {
        $this->readOnlyProperty = $value; // 错误: 不应对只读属性赋值
    }
}
'''  

##### 正确示例
'''php
class MyClass {
    /** @var string */
    private readonly string $readOnlyProperty;

    public function __construct(string $value) {
        $this->readOnlyProperty = $value; // 正确的用法是在构造函数中进行赋值
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule detects cases where an assignment operation is performed on read-only properties, which is typically a logical error.

##### Rule Meaning
In object-oriented programming, properties declared as read-only should generally not be modified externally. Attempting to assign a value to such properties could lead to unexpected behavior, thereby affecting the stability and maintainability of the code.

##### Error Example
'''php
class MyClass {
    /** @var string */
    private readonly string $readOnlyProperty;

    public function __construct(string $value) {
        $this->readOnlyProperty = $value; // Error: Should not assign a value to a read-only property
    }
}
'''  

##### Correct Example
'''php
class MyClass {
    /** @var string */
    private readonly string $readOnlyProperty;

    public function __construct(string $value) {
