    }
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则旨在警告开发者在 PHP 中使用赋值操作符时可能导致的不安全或不明确的代码。使用不当可能会导致逻辑错误或维护困难。

##### 规则意义
不恰当的赋值操作符使用可能会造成意想不到的结果，例如在条件语句中将赋值与比较混淆。这可能导致程序的逻辑出现错乱，增加了代码出错的风险，降低了代码的可维护性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
if ($a = 10) {
    // 此处实际上是赋值，而非比较
    echo 'a is 10';
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
if ($a == 10) {
    // 正确使用比较操作符
    echo 'a is 10';
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule aims to warn developers about potentially unsafe or ambiguous code that may result from using the assignment operator in PHP. Improper use can lead to logical errors or maintenance difficulties.

##### Rule Significance
Inappropriate use of the assignment operator may cause unexpected results, such as confusing assignment with comparison in conditional statements. This can lead to logic breakdowns in the program, increasing the risk of errors in the code and reducing its maintainability.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
if ($a = 10) {
    // This is actually an assignment, not a comparison
    echo 'a is 10';
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
if ($a == 10) {
    // Correct use of the comparison operator
    echo 'a is 10';
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则用于检查类属性是否被标记为抽象。

##### 规则意义
标记类属性为抽象可以明确表明该属性未在基类中实现，期望在子类中进行实现。此规则旨在提醒开发人员注意抽象类的设计，以确保代码的可维护性和清晰度。

##### 错误示例
'''php
abstract class BaseClass {
    abstract protected $property;
}

class ChildClass extends BaseClass {
    // 缺少对 $property 的实现
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
abstract class BaseClass {
    abstract protected $property;
}

class ChildClass extends BaseClass {
    protected $property = 'value'; // 正确地实现了抽象属性
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule checks whether class properties are marked as abstract.

##### Rule Meaning
Marking class properties as abstract clearly indicates that the property has not been implemented in the base class and is expected to be implemented in subclasses. This rule aims to remind developers to pay attention to the design of abstract classes to ensure the maintainability and clarity of the code.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
abstract class BaseClass {
    abstract protected $property;
}

class ChildClass extends BaseClass {
    // Missing implementation of $property
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
abstract class BaseClass {
    abstract protected $property;
}

class ChildClass extends BaseClass {
    protected $property = 'value'; // Correctly implements the abstract property
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则用于检查PHP代码中是否在适当的类上使用属性。

##### 规则意义
缺少适当的属性声明可能导致代码不易于理解和维护，同时增加了出现错误的概率。确保类中的属性被正确定义是良好的编程习惯。

##### 错误示例
'''php
class User {
    public $name;
    public $age;

    // 没有使用属性声明
    public function setName($name) {
        $this->name = $name;
    }
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
class User {
    private string $name;
    private int $age;

    public function setName(string $name): void {
        $this->name = $name;
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is used to check whether properties are used appropriately in PHP classes.

##### Rule Meaning
Missing proper property declarations can lead to code that is difficult to understand and maintain, while also increasing the likelihood of errors. Ensuring that properties in a class are correctly defined is a good programming practice.

##### Error Example
'''php
class User {
    public $name;
    public $age;

    // Property declaration is not used
    public function setName($name) {
        $this->name = $name;
    }
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
class User {
    private string $name;
    private int $age;

    public function setName(string $name): void {
        $this->name = $name;
    }
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在PHP中，属性通常不应通过公共构造函数进行初始化。这可能会导致类的设计不明确，也可能会让属性在不适当的情况下被修改。

##### 规则意义
确保属性的构造函数设置为非公共可以防止外部代码错误地修改属性，这样可以提高代码的封装性和可维护性。

##### 错误示例
```php
class Example {
    public int $value;

    public function __construct(int $value) {
        $this->value = $value;
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```php
class Example {
    private int $value;

    public function __construct(int $value) {
        $this->value = $value;
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In PHP, properties should generally not be initialized through public constructors. This can lead to unclear class design and may allow properties to be modified inappropriately.

##### Rule Meaning
Ensuring that the constructor for properties is non-public can prevent external code from incorrectly modifying these properties, thereby improving the encapsulation and maintainability of the code.

##### Incorrect Example
```php
class Example {
    public int $value;

    public function __construct(int $value) {
        $this->value = $value;
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```php
class Example {
    private int $value;

    public function __construct(int $value) {
        $this->value = $value;
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则用于检测代码中使用的已弃用属性。

##### 规则意义
使用已弃用的属性可能导致代码在未来版本中失效或引发不必要的错误，因此标记和修复这些属性是保持代码健康的重要部分。

##### 错误示例
'''php
class Example {
    #[Obsolete]
    public $deprecatedProperty;
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
class Example {
    // 使用新属性代替已弃用属性
    #[NewAttribute]
    public $newProperty;
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is used to detect deprecated attributes used in the code.

##### Rule Significance
Using deprecated attributes may cause code to fail or result in unnecessary errors in future versions, so marking and fixing these attributes is an important part of maintaining code health.

##### Incorrect Example
