}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则要求使用枚举类型的属性，以确保代码的可读性和一致性。

##### 规则意义
使用枚举型属性可以避免使用常量值，这样可以提高代码的安全性和可维护性，并增强代码的自文件化程度。

##### 错误示例
```php
class User {
    public $status;

    public function setStatus($status) {
        $this->status = $status;
    }
}

$user = new User();
$user->setStatus('active'); // 随意使用字符串作为状态
```

##### 正确示例
```php
enum UserStatus: string {
    case ACTIVE = 'active';
    case INACTIVE = 'inactive';
}

class User {
    public UserStatus $status;

    public function setStatus(UserStatus $status) {
        $this->status = $status;
    }
}

$user = new User();
$user->setStatus(UserStatus::ACTIVE); // 使用定义好的枚举状态
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule requires the use of enumeration types for properties to ensure code readability and consistency.

##### Rule Significance
Using enumeration properties can avoid the use of constant values, which enhances code safety and maintainability, and improves the self-documenting nature of the code.

##### Incorrect Example
```php
class User {
    public $status;

    public function setStatus($status) {
        $this->status = $status;
    }
}

$user = new User();
$user->setStatus('active'); // Arbitrarily using a string as status
```

##### Correct Example
```php
enum UserStatus: string {
    case ACTIVE = 'active';
    case INACTIVE = 'inactive';
}

class User {
    public UserStatus $status;

    public function setStatus(UserStatus $status) {
        $this->status = $status;
    }
}

$user = new User();
$user->setStatus(UserStatus::ACTIVE); // Using the defined enumeration status
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在PHP中，推荐使用接口(attribute)来定义对象的行为，以增强代码的可维护性和可扩展性。

##### 规则意义
使用接口可以降低类之间的耦合，提高代码的灵活性和复用性。避免直接使用属性可以减少意外修改带来的错误，有助于实现面向接口编程。

##### 错误示例
'''php
class User {
    public string $name;
    public int $age;
}

$user = new User();
$user->name = 'John';
$user->age = 30;
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
interface UserInterface {
    public function getName(): string;
    public function getAge(): int;
}

class User implements UserInterface {
    private string $name;
    private int $age;

    public function __construct(string $name, int $age) {
        $this->name = $name;
        $this->age = $age;
    }

    public function getName(): string {
        return $this->name;
    }

    public function getAge(): int {
        return $this->age;
    }
}

$user = new User('John', 30);
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In PHP, it is recommended to use interfaces (attributes) to define the behavior of objects, which enhances code maintainability and expandability.

##### Rule Significance
Using interfaces can reduce coupling between classes and improve the flexibility and reusability of the code. Avoiding direct use of properties can minimize errors caused by accidental modifications, aiding in the implementation of interface-oriented programming.

##### Error Example
'''php
class User {
    public string $name;
    public int $age;
}

$user = new User();
$user->name = 'John';
$user->age = 30;
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
interface UserInterface {
    public function getName(): string;
    public function getAge(): int;
}

class User implements UserInterface {
    private string $name;
    private int $age;

    public function __construct(string $name, int $age) {
        $this->name = $name;
        $this->age = $age;
    }

    public function getName(): string {
        return $this->name;
    }

    public function getAge(): int {
        return $this->age;
    }
}

$user = new User('John', 30);
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
