}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
trait Logger {
    public function log($message) {
        echo $message;
    }
}

class User {
    use Logger; // 正确：只使用一次trait
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In PHP, traits are used for code reuse. Improper use may lead to increased complexity and decreased maintainability of the code.

##### Rule Importance
Ensure that traits are used appropriately when designing classes to maintain code clarity and maintainability.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
trait Logger {
    public function log($message) {
        echo $message;
    }
}

class User {
    use Logger, Logger; // Error: Duplicate use of the same trait
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
trait Logger {
    public function log($message) {
        echo $message;
    }
}

class User {
    use Logger; // Correct: The trait is used only once
}
'''

rules.content:
