此规则旨在帮助开发者发现代码中不必要的条件判断，从而提高代码的可读性和维护性，避免潜在的逻辑错误。

##### 错误示例
'''php
if ($condition || true) {
    // 这段代码永远会执行，因为右侧是常量true。
    echo 'Always true';
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
if ($condition) {
    // 正常处理条件
    echo 'Condition met';
}
'''

在这个示例中，去掉了永远为真的条件，使得代码更简洁。

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
When performing Boolean operations, if the right side of the operation is always true, that part is redundant.

##### Rule Meaning
This rule aims to help developers identify unnecessary conditional checks in the code, thereby improving code readability and maintainability, and avoiding potential logical errors.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
if ($condition || true) {
    // This code will always execute because the right side is the constant true.
    echo 'Always true';
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
if ($condition) {
    // Normal condition handling
    echo 'Condition met';
}
'''

In this example, the always-true condition has been removed, making the code more concise.

