rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则检查代码中是否存在不当的类型转换为字符串操作，以确保代码在处理数据时能够保持一致性和准确性。

##### 规则意义
不当的字符串转换可能导致潜在的数据丢失或意外的行为，尤其是在处理复杂数据类型时。通过遵循此规则，可以提高代码的质量和可维护性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
$value = 123;
$stringValue = (string) $value;
$valueArray = [1, 2, 3];
$stringArray = (string) $valueArray; // 不恰当的转换
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
$value = 123;
$stringValue = (string) $value;
$valueArray = [1, 2, 3];
$stringArray = implode(',', $valueArray); // 正确的转换方式
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule checks for improper type conversions to string in the code to ensure consistency and accuracy when handling data.

##### Significance of the Rule
Improper string conversions can lead to potential data loss or unexpected behavior, especially when dealing with complex data types. By following this rule, the quality and maintainability of the code can be improved.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
$value = 123;
$stringValue = (string) $value;
$valueArray = [1, 2, 3];
$stringArray = (string) $valueArray; // Improper conversion
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
$value = 123;
$stringValue = (string) $value;
$valueArray = [1, 2, 3];
$stringArray = implode(',', $valueArray); // Correct conversion method
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在捕获异常时，如果异常已经在之前的捕获块中处理过，重复捕获将导致代码冗余，增加了维护成本。

##### 规则意义
保证代码的简洁与可维护性，避免重复捕获已处理的异常以降低潜在的错误和混淆。

##### 错误示例
```php
try {
    // 一些代码
} catch (Exception $e) {
    // 处理异常
}

try {
    // 一些其他代码
} catch (Exception $e) {
    // 不必要的再次处理相同异常
}
```

##### 正确示例
```php
try {
    // 一些代码
} catch (Exception $e) {
    // 正确处理异常
}
// 不再重复捕获相同的异常
``

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
When catching exceptions, if an exception has already been handled in a previous catch block, redundant catching will lead to code redundancy and increase maintenance costs.

##### Rule Significance
Ensures code simplicity and maintainability, avoiding the redundant catching of already handled exceptions to reduce potential errors and confusion.

##### Incorrect Example
```php
try {
    // Some code
} catch (Exception $e) {
    // Handle exception
}

try {
    // Some other code
} catch (Exception $e) {
    // Unnecessary re-handling of the same exception
}
```

##### Correct Example
```php
try {
    // Some code
} catch (Exception $e) {
    // Properly handle exception
}
// No longer redundantly catching the same exception
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则指出在代码中存在捕获未抛出的异常的情况，通常表明代码逻辑存在问题。

##### 规则意义
捕获未抛出的异常会使得代码变得冗余和难以维护，同时可能会导致理解上的混淆，影响代码的质量。确保只捕获在代码执行过程中可能被抛出的异常，有助于提高代码的可读性和可维护性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
try {
    // 不会抛出异常的代码块
} catch (Exception $e) {
    // 捕获了未抛出的异常
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
try {
    // 可能会抛出异常的代码块
    throw new Exception('An error occurred');
} catch (Exception $e) {
    // 正确捕获异常
    echo $e->getMessage();
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule points out the presence of catching exceptions that were not thrown in the code, which usually indicates a problem with the code logic.

##### Rule Meaning
Catching exceptions that have not been thrown can make the code redundant and difficult to maintain, and may lead to confusion in understanding, impacting the quality of the code. Ensuring that only exceptions that may be thrown during the execution of the code are caught helps improve the readability and maintainability of the code.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
try {
    // Code block that will not throw an exception
} catch (Exception $e) {
    // Caught an exception that was not thrown
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
try {
    // Code block that may throw an exception
    throw new Exception('An error occurred');
} catch (Exception $e) {
    // Correctly caught an exception
    echo $e->getMessage();
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在 PHP 中，当使用 `catch` 语句捕获异常时，需要提供一个变量来接收异常对象。非捕获异常（即没有捕获变量的 `catch` 语句）是不被支持的，可能会导致代码行为不符合预期。

##### 规则意义
确保在捕获异常时提供一个变量以接收异常对象，以便能够进行适当地处理和调试。未捕获的异常信息可能会丢失，导致难以追踪的问题。

##### 错误示例
```php
try {
    // 代码逻辑
} catch (Exception) {
    // 没有捕获变量
}
```

##### 正确示例
```php
try {
    // 代码逻辑
} catch (Exception $e) {
    // 使用捕获的异常对象
    echo $e->getMessage();
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In PHP, when using the `catch` statement to catch exceptions, it is necessary to provide a variable to receive the exception object. Uncaught exceptions (i.e., `catch` statements without a catch variable) are not supported and may lead to unexpected behavior in the code.

##### Rule Significance
Ensure that a variable is provided to receive the exception object when catching exceptions so that appropriate handling and debugging can be performed. Uncaught exception information may be lost, making it difficult to trace issues.

##### Error Example
```php
try {
    // 代码逻辑
} catch (Exception) {
    // 没有捕获变量
}
```

##### Correct Example
```php
try {
    // 代码逻辑
} catch (Exception $e) {
    // 使用捕获的异常对象
    echo $e->getMessage();
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在PHP中，`catch`语句只能捕获`Throwable`类型的对象，包括`Error`和`Exception`。该规则提醒开发者在`catch`语句中捕获非`Throwable`类型的对象，这会导致未定义的行为。

##### 规则意义
使用不当的`catch`语句可能会导致程序在遇到错误或异常时无法正确处理，并可能导致潜在的安全漏洞或程序崩溃。遵循这一规则能够提高代码的可靠性和稳定性。

##### 错误示例
```php
try {
    // ... 可能抛出异常的代码
} catch (Exception $e) {
    // ... 处理异常
} catch (int $code) { // 错误示例: 捕获int类型
    // 错误处理逻辑
}
```

##### 正确示例
```php
try {
    // ... 可能抛出异常的代码
} catch (Throwable $e) {
    // ... 处理所有可抛出的异常
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In PHP, the `catch` statement can only capture objects of type `Throwable`, which includes `Error` and `Exception`. This rule alerts developers to the capture of non-`Throwable` type objects in a `catch` statement, which can lead to undefined behavior.

##### Rule Significance
Improper use of `catch` statements may result in the program being unable to handle errors or exceptions correctly, potentially leading to security vulnerabilities or program crashes. Adhering to this rule can enhance the reliability and stability of the code.

##### Error Example
```php
try {
    // ... Code that may throw an exception
} catch (Exception $e) {
    // ... Handle the exception
} catch (int $code) { // Error Example: Capturing int type
    // Error handling logic
}
```

##### Correct Example
```php
try {
    // ... Code that may throw an exception
} catch (Throwable $e) {
    // ... Handle all throwables
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则旨在防止在类中使用动态属性，尤其是只读类应该避免使用动态属性，以保持类的封装性和可维护性。

##### 规则意义
动态属性可能会导致代码的不可预测性和难以维护的问题。限制动态属性的使用可以提高代码的可读性和稳定性。尤其是在只读类中，这种做法能够确保所有属性在类定义时都是明确的，有助于避免潜在错误。

##### 错误示例
'''php
class User
{
    public string $name;

    public function __construct(string $name)
    {
        $this->name = $name;
    }
}

$user = new User('Alice');
$user->age = 30; // 动态添加属性，不符合设计
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
class User
{
    public string $name;
    public int $age;

    public function __construct(string $name, int $age)
    {
        $this->name = $name;
        $this->age = $age;
    }
}

$user = new User('Alice', 30); // 所有属性在类定义时明确
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is aimed at preventing the use of dynamic properties within classes, especially in read-only classes, to maintain encapsulation and maintainability.

##### Significance of the Rule
Dynamic properties can lead to unpredictability and maintenance issues in code. Limiting the use of dynamic properties can enhance the readability and stability of the code. Especially in read-only classes, this practice ensures that all properties are explicit at the time of class definition, helping to avoid potential errors.

##### Error Example
'''php
class User
{
    public string $name;

    public function __construct(string $name)
    {
        $this->name = $name;
    }
}

$user = new User('Alice');
$user->age = 30; // Dynamically adding a property, not conforming to design
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
class User
{
    public string $name;
    public int $age;

    public function __construct(string $name, int $age)
    {
        $this->name = $name;
        $this->age = $age;
    }
}

$user = new User('Alice', 30); // All properties are explicit at class definition
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则检查类中是否存在重复定义的常量。

##### 规则意义
在一个类中定义重复的常量会导致代码的混淆和维护困难，可能会引入不必要的错误。在使用常量时，开发者可能会使用到重复定义的常量而导致意外行为，因此应避免此类情况。 

##### 错误示例
```php
class MyClass {
    const VALUE = 1;
    const VALUE = 2; // 重复定义
}
```

##### 正确示例
```php
class MyClass {
    const VALUE_ONE = 1;
    const VALUE_TWO = 2; // 使用了不同的常量名
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule checks for duplicate constant definitions within a class.

##### Rule Meaning
Defining duplicate constants within a class can lead to confusion and difficulties in maintenance, potentially introducing unnecessary errors. When using constants, developers may unintentionally use duplicate definitions, leading to unexpected behavior; therefore, such situations should be avoided.

##### Error Example
```php
class MyClass {
    const VALUE = 1;
    const VALUE = 2; // Duplicate definition
}
```

##### Correct Example
```php
class MyClass {
    const VALUE_ONE = 1;
    const VALUE_TWO = 2; // Different constant names used
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则检查PHP枚举类中是否定义了重复的成员名称。

##### 规则意义
枚举用于定义一组命名常量。在枚举定义中，若存在重复的成员名称，将导致潜在的逻辑错误，影响代码的可维护性和正确性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
enum Status {
    case PENDING;
    case COMPLETED;
    case PENDING; // 重复定义
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
enum Status {
    case PENDING;
    case COMPLETED;
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule checks for duplicate member names defined in PHP enum classes.

##### Rule Significance
Enums are used to define a set of named constants. If there are duplicate member names within an enum definition, it can lead to potential logical errors, affecting the maintainability and correctness of the code.

##### Error Example
'''php
enum Status {
    case PENDING;
    case COMPLETED;
    case PENDING; // Duplicate definition
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
enum Status {
    case PENDING;
    case COMPLETED;
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则检测类中是否存在重复的方法定义。方法名相同且参数签名相同的方法在同一个类中是不允许存在的。

##### 规则意义
重复的方法定义会导致代码可读性差，维护成本增加，并且可能会引发潜在的逻辑错误。在代码审查时，这类问题往往被忽视，但它们会对代码的长期维护产生负面影响。

##### 错误示例
'''php
class Example {
    public function test() {
        return 1;
    }

    public function test() {
        return 2;
    }
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
class Example {
    public function testOne() {
        return 1;
    }

    public function testTwo() {
        return 2;
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule detects whether there are duplicate method definitions within a class. Methods with the same name and parameter signature are not allowed to exist within the same class.

##### Rule Significance
Duplicate method definitions can lead to poor code readability, increased maintenance costs, and may trigger potential logical errors. During code reviews, such issues are often overlooked, but they can have a negative impact on the long-term maintenance of the code.

##### Error Example
'''php
class Example {
    public function test() {
        return 1;
    }

    public function test() {
        return 2;
    }
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
class Example {
    public function testOne() {
        return 1;
    }

    public function testTwo() {
        return 2;
    }
}
'''

