rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则旨在警告开发人员不要继承已废弃的类，以避免使用可能会导致不稳定或不兼容的功能。

##### 规则意义
继承已废弃类会导致代码的不稳定性和向后兼容性问题。使用这些类可能会在未来的版本中引入错误或移除相关功能，从而影响整个应用的运行。

##### 错误示例
'''php
class DeprecatedClass {
    // 某些已被废弃的方法
}

class MyClass extends DeprecatedClass {
    // 依赖已废弃类的方法
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
class MyClass {
    public function newMethod() {
        // 使用新的、推荐的方法
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule aims to warn developers against inheriting deprecated classes to avoid using features that may lead to instability or incompatibility.

##### Significance of the Rule
Inheriting deprecated classes can lead to code instability and backward compatibility issues. Utilizing these classes may introduce bugs or remove related functionalities in future versions, thereby affecting the entire application's operation.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
class DeprecatedClass {
    // Some deprecated methods
}

class MyClass extends DeprecatedClass {
    // Dependent on methods from deprecated class
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
class MyClass {
    public function newMethod() {
        // Use new, recommended methods
    }
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在PHP中，枚举类（Enum）是一种特殊的类，它用于表示一组有限的常量。当一个类扩展枚举类时，可能会违反枚举的设计意图。

##### 规则意义
扩展枚举类可能导致代码的可维护性和一致性受到影响。枚举类应该被用作固定的常量集，而不是作为其他类的基类。

##### 错误示例
```php
enum Status {
    case PENDING;
    case COMPLETED;
}

class Order extends Status {
    // 错误：不应扩展枚举类
}
```

##### 正确示例
```php
enum Status {
    case PENDING;
    case COMPLETED;
}

class Order {
    private Status $status;

    public function __construct(Status $status) {
        $this->status = $status;
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In PHP, an enum class is a special type of class used to represent a finite set of constants. Extending an enum class may violate the intended design of enums.

##### Rule Significance
Extending an enum class may compromise the maintainability and consistency of the code. Enum classes should be used as fixed sets of constants rather than as base classes for other classes.

##### Incorrect Example
```php
enum Status {
    case PENDING;
    case COMPLETED;
}

class Order extends Status {
    // Error: Should not extend an enum class
}
```

##### Correct Example
```php
enum Status {
    case PENDING;
    case COMPLETED;
}

class Order {
    private Status $status;

    public function __construct(Status $status) {
        $this->status = $status;
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则旨在防止类继承最终类（final class），因为最终类不允许被继承。尝试继承最终类会导致运算时错误。

##### 规则意义
在PHP中，定义为final的类是不可被其他类继承的。如果一个类意图被设计为最终的，允许其子类可能导致不必要的复杂性和潜在错误，代码的意图不明确，因此在设计上可能有违最佳实践。

##### 错误示例
```php
final class FinalClass {
    // 代码
}

class SubClass extends FinalClass {
    // 试图继承最终类
}
```

##### 正确示例
```php
final class FinalClass {
    // 代码
}

// 不应尝试继承最终类
// class SubClass extends FinalClass {
// }
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule aims to prevent class inheritance of final classes, as final classes are not allowed to be inherited. Attempting to inherit a final class will result in a runtime error.

##### Rule Significance
In PHP, a class defined as final cannot be inherited by other classes. If a class is intended to be final, allowing its subclasses may lead to unnecessary complexity and potential errors, making the intent of the code unclear, and thus may violate best practices in design.

##### Incorrect Example
```php
final class FinalClass {
    // code
}

class SubClass extends FinalClass {
    // attempting to inherit a final class
}
```

##### Correct Example
```php
final class FinalClass {
    // code
}

// Do not attempt to inherit a final class
// class SubClass extends FinalClass {
// }
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
类必须实现其声明的所有接口方法，以确保接口契约的完整性。

##### 规则意义
当一个类声明实现某个接口时，它必须实现该接口中的所有方法。未实现的方法将导致代码逻辑的不完整，可能导致运行时错误。

##### 错误示例
'''php
interface SomeInterface {
    public function methodOne();
    public function methodTwo();
}

class SomeClass implements SomeInterface {
    public function methodOne() {
        // 实现代码
    }
    // methodTwo没有实现
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
interface SomeInterface {
    public function methodOne();
    public function methodTwo();
}

class SomeClass implements SomeInterface {
    public function methodOne() {
        // 实现代码
    }
    public function methodTwo() {
        // 实现代码
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
A class must implement all methods declared in its interfaces to ensure the completeness of the interface contract.

##### Rule Significance
When a class declares that it implements an interface, it must implement all methods within that interface. Unimplemented methods will lead to incomplete code logic, potentially resulting in runtime errors.

##### Error Example
'''php
interface SomeInterface {
    public function methodOne();
    public function methodTwo();
}

class SomeClass implements SomeInterface {
    public function methodOne() {
        // Implementation code
    }
    // methodTwo is not implemented
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
interface SomeInterface {
    public function methodOne();
    public function methodTwo();
}

class SomeClass implements SomeInterface {
    public function methodOne() {
        // Implementation code
    }
    public function methodTwo() {
        // Implementation code
    }
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在PHP中，Nette的Object类已被弃用，允许扩展该类可能导致不必要的兼容性问题。

##### 规则意义
避免扩展Nette的Object类可以提高代码的质量和兼容性，鼓励使用更现代的PHP特性，如Trait和接口。

##### 错误示例
'''php
class MyClass extends Nettebject {
    // 业务逻辑
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
class MyClass {
    // 业务逻辑
}

// 使用Trait来实现设计模式或者功能
trait MyTrait {
    // Trait中的方法
}

class AnotherClass {
    use MyTrait;
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In PHP, the Nette Object class has been deprecated, and extending this class may lead to unnecessary compatibility issues.

##### Rule Significance
Avoiding the extension of the Nette Object class can enhance code quality and compatibility, encouraging the use of more modern PHP features such as Traits and interfaces.

##### Error Example
'''php
class MyClass extends Nettebject {
    // Business logic
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
class MyClass {
    // Business logic
}

// Use Traits to implement design patterns or functionality
trait MyTrait {
    // Methods in the Trait
}

class AnotherClass {
    use MyTrait;
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则用于检测类是否正确扩展Trait，确保Trait的使用符合PHP的最佳实践。

##### 规则意义
在PHP中，Trait用于实现代码复用，但滥用Trait或错误地扩展Trait可能导致代码可维护性差和潜在的错误。使用此规则可以帮助开发者确认类和Trait的关系是否符合预期，并避免一些常见的问题。

##### 错误示例
'''php
trait SampleTrait {
    public function sampleMethod() {
        return 'Hello from Trait!';
    }
}

class SampleClass extends SampleTrait {
    // 错误：类不能扩展Traits
}
''' 

##### 正确示例
'''php
trait SampleTrait {
    public function sampleMethod() {
        return 'Hello from Trait!';
    }
}

class SampleClass {
    use SampleTrait;
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is used to detect whether a class correctly extends a Trait, ensuring that the use of Traits complies with PHP best practices.

##### Significance of the Rule
In PHP, Traits are used to achieve code reuse, but improper use of Traits or incorrectly extending Traits can lead to poor code maintainability and potential errors. Using this rule can help developers confirm that the relationship between classes and Traits meets expectations and avoid common issues.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
trait SampleTrait {
    public function sampleMethod() {
        return 'Hello from Trait!';
    }
}

class SampleClass extends SampleTrait {
    // Error: classes cannot extend Traits
}
''' 

##### Correct Example
'''php
trait SampleTrait {
    public function sampleMethod() {
        return 'Hello from Trait!';
    }
}

class SampleClass {
    use SampleTrait;
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则用于检测实现了已经被标记为过时的接口的类。

##### 规则意义
实现过时接口的类可能会导致与未来版本的不兼容，并可能使代码维护变得困难。遵循现代接口设计的最佳实践，有助于提高代码的可维护性和可扩展性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
interface OldInterface {
    public function oldMethod();
}

class DeprecatedClass implements OldInterface {
    public function oldMethod() {
        // 实现过时接口的方法
    }
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
interface NewInterface {
    public function newMethod();
}

class CurrentClass implements NewInterface {
    public function newMethod() {
        // 实现新的接口的方法
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is used to detect classes that implement interfaces that have been marked as deprecated.

##### Rule Significance
Classes that implement deprecated interfaces may lead to incompatibility with future versions and can make code maintenance difficult. Adhering to best practices in modern interface design helps improve the maintainability and extensibility of the code.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
interface OldInterface {
    public function oldMethod();
}

class DeprecatedClass implements OldInterface {
    public function oldMethod() {
        // Implementation of the deprecated interface method
    }
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
interface NewInterface {
    public function newMethod();
}

class CurrentClass implements NewInterface {
    public function newMethod() {
        // Implementation of the new interface method
    }
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在定义一个类时，如果该类没有声明基类进行扩展，可能导致代码可重用性差，无法享受继承带来的多态性和其他对象导向特性。

##### 规则意义
确保所有类定义都有合理的父类继承，可以提高代码的扩展性和维护性，避免不必要的重复代码，提升整体代码质量。

##### 错误示例
'''php
class MyClass {
    public function myMethod() {
        return 'Hello, World!';
    }
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
class BaseClass {
    public function baseMethod() {
        return 'Base Method';
    }
}

class MyClass extends BaseClass {
    public function myMethod() {
        return 'Hello, World!';
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
When defining a class, if the class does not declare a base class for extension, it may lead to poor code reusability, preventing the enjoyment of polymorphism and other object-oriented features.

##### Rule Meaning
Ensuring that all class definitions have reasonable parent class inheritance can enhance code extensibility and maintainability, avoid unnecessary duplicate code, and improve overall code quality.

##### Error Example
'''php
class MyClass {
    public function myMethod() {
        return 'Hello, World!';
    }
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
class BaseClass {
    public function baseMethod() {
        return 'Base Method';
    }
}

class MyClass extends BaseClass {
    public function myMethod() {
        return 'Hello, World!';
    }
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则检查类是否实现了所有声明的接口方法。

##### 规则意义
实现接口是面向对象编程的重要组成部分，缺失接口方法的实现会导致代码不符合预期，并可能在运行时引发错误。确保所有接口都被正确实现，使得代码更加可靠和可维护。

##### 错误示例
```php
interface SampleInterface {
    public function someMethod();
}

class SampleClass implements SampleInterface {
    // 缺失 someMethod 方法的实现
}
```

##### 正确示例
```php
interface SampleInterface {
    public function someMethod();
}

class SampleClass implements SampleInterface {
    public function someMethod() {
        // 方法实现
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule checks whether a class implements all the declared interface methods.

##### Rule Significance
Implementing interfaces is an important part of object-oriented programming. Missing implementations of interface methods can lead to code behaving unexpectedly and may cause runtime errors. Ensuring that all interfaces are correctly implemented makes the code more reliable and maintainable.

##### Error Example
```php
interface SampleInterface {
    public function someMethod();
}

class SampleClass implements SampleInterface {
    // Missing implementation of someMethod
}
```

##### Correct Example
```php
interface SampleInterface {
    public function someMethod();
}

class SampleClass implements SampleInterface {
    public function someMethod() {
        // Method implementation
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则用于确保类名遵循命名约定，通常要求采用 PascalCase 命名法。

##### 规则意义
遵循一致的命名规则可以提高代码的可读性和可维护性。使用 PascalCase 命名法可以帮助开发者快速识别类定义，并使代码更具专业性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
class myclass {
    // 错误：类名应该使用 PascalCase
}

class user_profile {
    // 错误：类名应该使用 PascalCase
}
''' 

##### 正确示例
'''php
class MyClass {
    // 正确：类名符合 PascalCase 命名法
}

class UserProfile {
    // 正确：类名符合 PascalCase 命名法
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is used to ensure that class names follow naming conventions, which typically require the use of PascalCase.

##### Rule Meaning
Following consistent naming conventions can improve the readability and maintainability of code. Using PascalCase can help developers quickly identify class definitions and make the code appear more professional.

