rules.content:
#### 规则概述
当一个类需要被序列化时，它应该实现\`Serializable\`接口，以确保序列化和反序列化的过程正确。

##### 规则意义
实现\`Serializable\`接口可以确保对象在序列化时包含完整状态，避免在反序列化时出现数据缺失或类型错误。这对于数据的持久化和传输至关重要。

##### 错误示例
'''php
class User {
    private $name;
    private $age;

    public function __construct($name, $age) {
        $this->name = $name;
        $this->age = $age;
    }
}

$user = new User('Alice', 30);
$serialized = serialize($user);
''' 

##### 正确示例
'''php
class User implements Serializable {
    private $name;
    private $age;

    public function __construct($name, $age) {
        $this->name = $name;
        $this->age = $age;
    }

    public function serialize() {
        return serialize([$this->name, $this->age]);
    }

    public function unserialize($data) {
        list($this->name, $this->age) = unserialize($data);
    }
}

$user = new User('Alice', 30);
$serialized = serialize($user);
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Overview of Rules
When a class needs to be serialized, it should implement the `Serializable` interface to ensure that the serialization and deserialization processes are correct.

##### Significance of the Rule
Implementing the `Serializable` interface ensures that the object contains a complete state during serialization, preventing data loss or type errors during deserialization. This is crucial for data persistence and transmission.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
class User {
    private $name;
    private $age;

    public function __construct($name, $age) {
        $this->name = $name;
        $this->age = $age;
    }
}

$user = new User('Alice', 30);
$serialized = serialize($user);
''' 

##### Correct Example
'''php
class User implements Serializable {
    private $name;
    private $age;

    public function __construct($name, $age) {
        $this->name = $name;
        $this->age = $age;
    }

    public function serialize() {
        return serialize([$this->name, $this->age]);
    }

    public function unserialize($data) {
        list($this->name, $this->age) = unserialize($data);
    }
}

$user = new User('Alice', 30);
$serialized = serialize($user);
'''

