}

class MySubClass extends MyClass {
    // 不能重写SOME_CONSTANT，确保其安全性
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In PHP, class constants should be declared as `final` to maintain their immutability and prevent them from being overridden by subclasses.

