}

echo MyClass::MY_CONSTANT; // 正确引用，输出'value'
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is used to detect whether class constants referenced in the code exist. If the referenced class constant is not found, an error will be triggered.

##### Rule Meaning
Ensuring that the constants used in the code are valid improves code readability and maintainability and reduces the likelihood of runtime errors.

##### Error Example
