This rule aims to detect unused constants in classes.

##### Rule Significance
The primary purpose of defining constants is to enhance the readability and maintainability of the code. If a constant in a class is unused, it may indicate the presence of redundant code, leading to confusion in the codebase and increasing the cost of understanding.

