        return [self::VALUE_ONE, self::VALUE_TWO];
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule checks whether a PHP class implements an enum interface.

##### Rule Importance
Implementing an enum interface helps to provide readability and consistency, ensuring that the class follows specific behaviors and structures when dealing with enum types, thereby enhancing the maintainability and reliability of the code.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
class MyClass {
    // Does not implement any enum interface
}
'''

