rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在使用 Doctrine ORM 时，建议使用枚举类型来定义固定的集合值，以确保类型安全和代码可读性。

##### 规则意义
使用枚举类型可以减少代码中的硬编码字符串，提高可维护性，避免拼写错误和类型不匹配的问题。同时，有助于代码的自文档化，使其更容易理解。

##### 错误示例
'''php
// 错误示例: 使用硬编码字符串作为状态
class User {
    private string $status;

    public function setStatus(string $status) {
        $this->status = $status;
    }
}
// 使用时
$user->setStatus('active'); // 可能导致拼写错误
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
// 正确示例: 使用枚举类型来定义状态
enum UserStatus: string {
    case ACTIVE = 'active';
    case INACTIVE = 'inactive';
}

class User {
    private UserStatus $status;

    public function setStatus(UserStatus $status) {
        $this->status = $status;
    }
}
// 使用时
$user->setStatus(UserStatus::ACTIVE);
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
When using Doctrine ORM, it is recommended to use enum types to define fixed set values to ensure type safety and code readability.

##### Significance of the Rule
Using enum types can reduce hardcoded strings in the code, improve maintainability, and avoid issues with spelling errors and type mismatches. Additionally, it helps with self-documenting the code, making it easier to understand.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
// Incorrect Example: Using hardcoded strings as status
class User {
    private string $status;

    public function setStatus(string $status) {
        $this->status = $status;
    }
}
// Usage
$user->setStatus('active'); // May lead to spelling errors
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
// Correct Example: Using enum types to define status
enum UserStatus: string {
    case ACTIVE = 'active';
    case INACTIVE = 'inactive';
}

class User {
    private UserStatus $status;

    public function setStatus(UserStatus $status) {
        $this->status = $status;
    }
}
// Usage
$user->setStatus(UserStatus::ACTIVE);
'''

