rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule detects whether `==` comparisons in the code always return `true`.

##### Rule Meaning
Code where equality comparisons always evaluate to true often indicates a logical error or unnecessary complexity, which may lead to potential defects or misleading code behavior.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
if ($value == 1) {
    // This block of code will always execute
    echo 'This will always be executed';
}
'''

