##### Rule Significance
Using `==` for comparisons can trigger type conversion, resulting in logical errors. This rule aims to promote the use of strict comparisons (`===`) to avoid potential mistakes.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
$var1 = 0;
$var2 = '0';
if ($var1 == $var2) {
    echo '这两者相等';  // 这很容易生成误导性结果
}
'''

