'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在 interface 中定义的常量不应重复。

##### 规则意义
使用重复的常量会导致代码的可读性和可维护性降低，也可能造成潜在的逻辑错误。这条规则帮助确保常量在接口中是唯一的，从而提高代码的清晰度和质量。

##### 错误示例
```php
interface ExampleInterface {
    const VALUE = 1;
    const VALUE = 2; // 重复定义常量
}
```

##### 正确示例
```php
interface ExampleInterface {
    const VALUE_ONE = 1;
    const VALUE_TWO = 2; // 不重复定义
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
Constants defined in an interface should not be duplicated.

##### Rule Meaning
Using duplicate constants can reduce the readability and maintainability of the code and may cause potential logical errors. This rule helps ensure that constants in the interface are unique, thus improving the clarity and quality of the code.

##### Incorrect Example
```php
interface ExampleInterface {
    const VALUE = 1;
    const VALUE = 2; // Duplicate constant definition
}
```

##### Correct Example
```php
interface ExampleInterface {
    const VALUE_ONE = 1;
    const VALUE_TWO = 2; // No duplicate definition
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则用于检测 PHP 接口中是否存在重复的枚举值定义。

##### 规则意义
在定义接口的枚举类型时，重复的枚举值可能导致代码逻辑混乱，增加维护成本，甚至产生意想不到的错误。确保枚举值的唯一性可以提升代码的可读性和可靠性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
interface Status {
    const ACTIVE = 1;
    const INACTIVE = 0;
    const DISABLED = 1; // 这里的值与 ACTIVE 冲突
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
interface Status {
    const ACTIVE = 1;
    const INACTIVE = 0;
    const DISABLED = 2; // 正确的唯一值
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is used to detect the presence of duplicate enum value definitions in PHP interfaces.

##### Rule Significance
When defining enum types in interfaces, duplicate enum values can lead to disorganized code logic, increase maintenance costs, and even produce unexpected errors. Ensuring the uniqueness of enum values can improve code readability and reliability.

##### Error Example
'''php
interface Status {
    const ACTIVE = 1;
    const INACTIVE = 0;
    const DISABLED = 1; // The value here conflicts with ACTIVE
}
'''

##### Correct Example
