This rule checks for duplicate method definitions in an interface. An interface should not have multiple methods with the same name.

##### Rule Significance
Duplicate method definitions can reduce the readability and maintainability of the code, leading to confusion and errors. If an interface defines multiple methods with the same name, subsequent implementing classes may be unable to determine which method to use, resulting in unexpected behavior or errors.

##### Error Example
'''php
interface ExampleInterface {
    public function doSomething();
    public function doSomething();
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
interface CorrectExampleInterface {
    public function doSomething();
    public function doSomethingElse();
}
'''

rules.content:
