This rule detects whether there are duplicate property declarations in an interface, preventing type inconsistency caused by repeated definitions.

##### Significance of the Rule
Defining duplicate properties in an interface may lead to confusion, making it difficult for developers to clearly understand the structure of the interface, which may result in code errors and maintenance challenges.

