rules.content:
#### 规则概述
本规则旨在确保接口的实现类正确地使用Trait，以避免潜在的冲突和逻辑错误。

##### 规则意义
在PHP中，Trait作为代码复用机制，有时可能会与接口的实现产生冲突。如果一个类同时实现了某个接口并使用了Trait，Trait中的方法可能重写接口中的方法，导致接口契约的非预期行为。遵循此规则可以提高代码的可维护性和可读性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
interface Logger {
    public function log(string $message);
}

trait FileLogger {
    public function log(string $message) {
        // 文件记录日志
    }
}

class AppLogger implements Logger {
    use FileLogger;
    // 这里可能会引发接口和Trait之间的冲突
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
interface Logger {
    public function log(string $message);
}

trait FileLogger {
    // 保持Trait中的方法避免冲突
}

class AppLogger implements Logger {
    use FileLogger;
    public function log(string $message) {
        // 实现接口的方法，避免重写Trait中的方法
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule aims to ensure that implementing classes of interfaces correctly use Traits to avoid potential conflicts and logical errors.

##### Significance of the Rule
In PHP, Traits serve as a mechanism for code reuse, which can sometimes conflict with the implementation of interfaces. If a class implements an interface and uses a Trait simultaneously, methods in the Trait may override methods in the interface, leading to unexpected behavior of the interface contract. Following this rule can improve the maintainability and readability of the code.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
interface Logger {
    public function log(string $message);
}

trait FileLogger {
    public function log(string $message) {
        // File logging
    }
}

class AppLogger implements Logger {
    use FileLogger;
    // This may cause conflicts between the interface and the Trait
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
interface Logger {
    public function log(string $message);
}

trait FileLogger {
    // Keep the methods in the Trait to avoid conflicts
}

class AppLogger implements Logger {
    use FileLogger;
    public function log(string $message) {
        // Implement the method of the interface, avoiding overriding methods in the Trait
    }
}
'''

