This rule checks whether a variable has been properly set before it is used, aiming to avoid potential issues with undefined variable usage.

##### Rule Significance
In PHP, attempting to use an undefined variable may lead to errors or unexpected behavior. Therefore, it is considered good coding practice to ensure that a variable has been initialized or to check it using the `isset` function.

##### Error Example
'''php
if ($value) {
    echo $value;
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
$value = null;
if (isset($value)) {
