#### 规则概述
该规则检测代码中的逻辑与 (`&&`) 表达式总是返回 `false` 的情况。

##### 规则意义
逻辑与表达式的总为假可能表示存在逻辑错误，可能导致代码的执行路径不符合预期，最终影响软件的功能和可靠性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
if (false && $someCondition) {
    // 这一块代码永远不会被执行
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
if (true && $someCondition) {
    // 这个块代码只有在 $someCondition 为 true 时执行
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule detects cases where logical AND (`&&`) expressions in the code always evaluate to `false`.

##### Rule Meaning
An always-false logical AND expression may indicate a logical error, potentially leading to execution paths that do not behave as expected, ultimately affecting the functionality and reliability of the software.

##### Error Example
'''php
if (false && $someCondition) {
    // This block of code will never be executed
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
if (true && $someCondition) {
    // This block of code executes only when $someCondition is true
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在逻辑表达式中，使用逻辑“与”（&&）操作符时，如果一个表达式的值始终为 true，则整个表达式的结果也将始终为 true。

##### 规则意义
这种情况可能导致代码的可读性和可维护性降低，同时可能隐藏潜在的逻辑错误。开发者应该避免使用不必要的逻辑表达式，尤其是那些总是返回同一结果的表达式。清晰的代码结构会使维护更容易，并帮助其他开发者理解代码意图。

##### 错误示例
'''php
if (true && $someCondition) {
    // 这个条件总是为真，$someCondition 的结果将被忽略
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
if ($someCondition) {
    // 直接使用 $someCondition，逻辑更清晰
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In a logical expression, when using the logical "and" (&&) operator, if the value of one expression is always true, then the result of the entire expression will also always be true.

##### Rule Significance
This situation can lead to reduced code readability and maintainability, while potentially hiding underlying logical errors. Developers should avoid using unnecessary logical expressions, especially those that always return the same result. A clear code structure will make maintenance easier and help other developers understand the intent of the code.

##### Error Example
'''php
if (true && $someCondition) {
    // This condition is always true, and the result of $someCondition will be ignored
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
if ($someCondition) {
    // Directly using $someCondition, making the logic clearer
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则旨在检测逻辑与(`&&`)操作符左侧的表达式是否总是返回`false`，这种情况表明后续的代码逻辑可能是冗余的。

##### 规则意义
逻辑表达式中的某一部分总是为假，将导致整个逻辑表达式的结果无论右侧表达式是什么都为假。这可能会导致意外的逻辑错误，增加代码的复杂性与维护成本。

##### 错误示例
'''php
function checkValue($value) {
    if (false && $value > 10) {
        echo 'Value is greater than 10';
    }
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
function checkValue($value) {
    if ($value !== false && $value > 10) {
        echo 'Value is greater than 10';
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule aims to detect whether the expression on the left side of the logical AND (`&&`) operator always evaluates to `false`, indicating that the subsequent code logic may be redundant.

##### Rule Meaning
A part of a logical expression that is always false will cause the result of the entire logical expression to be false regardless of what the right-side expression is. This can lead to unexpected logical errors, increasing the complexity and maintenance costs of the code.

##### Error Example
'''php
function checkValue($value) {
    if (false && $value > 10) {
        echo 'Value is greater than 10';
    }
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
function checkValue($value) {
    if ($value !== false && $value > 10) {
        echo 'Value is greater than 10';
    }
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则用于检测逻辑与操作符（`&&`）左侧表达式总为真的情况。该情况可能导致代码逻辑不清晰或引起误解。

##### 规则意义
在代码中，如果逻辑与操作的左侧总是返回`true`，则右侧表达式的评估可能是不必要的，且可能导致不必要的计算或引起困惑，降低代码的可读性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
if (true && $condition) {
    // 处理条件
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
if ($condition) {
    // 处理条件
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is used to detect situations where the left side of a logical AND operator (`&&`) is always true. Such situations may lead to unclear code logic or misunderstandings.

##### Rule Meaning
In the code, if the left side of a logical AND operation always returns `true`, then the evaluation of the right side expression may be unnecessary, potentially leading to redundant computations or confusion, thus lowering code readability.

##### Error Example
'''php
if (true && $condition) {
    // Handle condition
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
if ($condition) {
    // Handle condition
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在PHP中，如果在逻辑与操作（`&&`）的结果上没有使用，可能会导致意图显示不清，代码可读性降低。

##### 规则意义
确保所有的逻辑运算结果都被适当地使用可以提高代码的可读性，减少潜在的错误，并帮助维护代码的质量。

##### 错误示例
```php
$condition1 = true;
$condition2 = false;

// 没有使用逻辑与的结果，可能导致代码意图不明
$condition1 && $condition2;
// 后续代码执行依赖于以上判断，但是并未明确使用结果
```

##### 正确示例
```php
$condition1 = true;
$condition2 = false;

// 正确使用逻辑与的结果
$result = $condition1 && $condition2;
if ($result) {
    // 执行相应的操作
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In PHP, if the result of a logical AND operation (`&&`) is not used, it can lead to unclear intentions and reduced code readability.

##### Rule Meaning
Ensuring that all logical operation results are appropriately used can enhance code readability, reduce potential errors, and help maintain code quality.

##### Error Example
```php
$condition1 = true;
$condition2 = false;

// The result of the logical AND is not used, which may lead to unclear intentions
$condition1 && $condition2;
// Subsequent code execution depends on the above judgment, but the result is not explicitly used
```

##### Correct Example
```php
$condition1 = true;
$condition2 = false;

// Properly using the result of the logical AND
$result = $condition1 && $condition2;
if ($result) {
    // Perform corresponding actions
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在逻辑与运算 (`&&`) 的右侧，若表达式常为 `false`，则意味着逻辑操作可能没有执行意义。

##### 规则意义
使用 `&&` 连接的条件表达式如果右侧总是 `false`，则左侧的表达式将会被忽略。这种情况可能会导致代码逻辑不明确，从而引发潜在缺陷，影响代码的可读性和可维护性。

##### 错误示例
```php
if ($condition1 && false) {
    // 此块代码永远不会被执行
}
```

##### 正确示例
```php
if ($condition1) {
    // 在这里处理 $condition1 为 true 的情况
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
On the right side of a logical AND operation (`&&`), if the expression is often `false`, it means the logical operation may have no execution significance.

##### Rule Meaning
If a conditional expression connected with `&&` always has `false` on the right side, the expression on the left will be ignored. This situation can lead to unclear code logic, potentially causing defects and affecting the readability and maintainability of the code.

##### Incorrect Example
```php
if ($condition1 && false) {
    // This block of code will never be executed
}
```

##### Correct Example
```php
if ($condition1) {
    // Handle the case where $condition1 is true here
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
当在逻辑与运算符`&&`的右侧条件总是返回`true`时，会导致左侧的条件部分失去实际意义。

##### 规则意义
逻辑运算符的正确使用可以提高代码的可读性和可维护性。如果某个条件永远为真，应该重新审视逻辑设计，避免代码的冗余。

##### 错误示例
```php
if ($a > 0 && true) {
    // 执行某些操作
}
```

##### 正确示例
```php
if ($a > 0) {
    // 执行某些操作
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
When the condition on the right side of the logical AND operator `&&` always returns `true`, the condition on the left side becomes meaningless.

##### Rule Significance
The correct use of logical operators can enhance the readability and maintainability of code. If a condition is always true, the logical design should be reconsidered to avoid redundancy in the code.

##### Incorrect Example
```php
if ($a > 0 && true) {
    // 执行某些操作
}
```

##### Correct Example
```php
if ($a > 0) {
    // 执行某些操作
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在逻辑或 (`||`) 操作中，如果左侧的条件总是为假，则其右侧的条件将永远不会被执行，这是不必要的代码，可能导致逻辑错误。

##### 规则意义
确保代码逻辑清晰且可维护，避免不必要的条件判断，以提高代码执行效率和可读性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
if (false || $value > 10) {
    // 这段代码永远会执行右侧的条件，因为左侧总为假
    echo "Value is greater than 10";
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
if ($value > 10) {
    echo "Value is greater than 10";
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In a logical OR (`||`) operation, if the left-side condition is always false, the right-side condition will never be executed. This results in unnecessary code, which may lead to logical errors.

##### Significance of the Rule
Ensure that the code logic is clear and maintainable, avoid unnecessary condition checks to improve code execution efficiency and readability.

##### Error Example
'''php
if (false || $value > 10) {
    // This code will always execute the right-side condition because the left side is always false
    echo "Value is greater than 10";
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
if ($value > 10) {
    echo "Value is greater than 10";
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则检测在逻辑或操作符（`||`）左侧总是返回 `true` 的表达式。

##### 规则意义
使用左侧总为真（`true`）的表达式可能会导致代码逻辑错误，因为右侧的条件将永远不会被检查。这可能导致程序的逻辑缺陷和潜在的错误。在编写更可读和可维护的代码时，应该警惕这一点。

##### 错误示例
'''php
if (true || $condition) {
    // 这段代码永远会执行
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
if ($condition) {
    // 仅在条件为真时执行
}
'''

##### 注意事项
确保在逻辑操作中使用真实的条件，而不是硬编码的布尔值。

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule detects expressions that always return `true` on the left side of the logical OR operator (`||`).

##### Rule Meaning
Using an expression that is always true on the left side may lead to logical errors in the code, as the condition on the right side will never be checked. This can result in logical flaws and potential bugs in the program. Attention should be paid to this when writing more readable and maintainable code.

##### Example of Error
'''php
if (true || $condition) {
    // This code will always execute
}
'''

##### Example of Correctness
'''php
if ($condition) {
    // Executes only when the condition is true
}
'''

##### Notes
Ensure that real conditions are used in logical operations, rather than hard-coded boolean values.

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则旨在检查逻辑运算符（如 `||` 和 `&&`）左侧的表达式是否为布尔类型，以确保逻辑运算的有效性。

##### 规则意义
在 PHP 中，逻辑运算符的左侧如果不是布尔值，则容易导致意想不到的结果。引入这种检查可以帮助开发者识别潜在的逻辑错误，确保代码逻辑清晰且可维护。

##### 错误示例
'''php
$foo = 10;
if ($foo || $bar) {
    // do something
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
$isLoggedIn = true;
if ($isLoggedIn || $bar) {
    // do something
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is designed to check whether the expression on the left side of logical operators (such as `||` and `&&`) is of boolean type, to ensure the validity of logical operations.

##### Rule Significance
In PHP, if the left side of a logical operator is not a boolean value, it can lead to unexpected results. Introducing this check can help developers identify potential logical errors and ensure that the code logic is clear and maintainable.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
$foo = 10;
if ($foo || $bar) {
    // do something
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
$isLoggedIn = true;
if ($isLoggedIn || $bar) {
    // do something
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
当逻辑或 (`||`) 操作符的结果没有被使用时，将会导致潜在的错误或不必要的代码复杂性。这种情况在某些情况下可能会导致难以检测的缺陷。

##### 规则意义
该规则的目的是确保开发者意识到逻辑或操作的结果未被利用，避免遗漏可能的逻辑错误，并提升代码的清晰度和可维护性。

##### 错误示例
```php
$isActive = true;
// 逻辑或的结果未被使用
$isActive || false;
```  

##### 正确示例
```php
$isActive = true;
// 正确使用逻辑或的结果
$result = $isActive || false;
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
When the result of a logical OR (`||`) operator is not utilized, it can lead to potential errors or unnecessary code complexity. In some cases, this situation may result in defects that are difficult to detect.

##### Rule Meaning
The purpose of this rule is to ensure that developers are aware that the result of the logical OR operation is not being used, to avoid missing potential logical errors, and to improve code clarity and maintainability.

##### Error Example
```php
$isActive = true;
// The result of the logical OR is not used
$isActive || false;
```  

##### Correct Example
```php
$isActive = true;
// Correctly using the result of the logical OR
$result = $isActive || false;
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则针对在逻辑或运算符右侧始终返回假值的情况进行检查。这种情况可能是逻辑错误，导致代码在实际运行时无法达到预期效果。

##### 规则意义
确保逻辑运算符的使用合乎逻辑，提高代码的正确性和可维护性。任何始终返回假的表达式都可能导致系统状态不正确，增加错误发生的风险。

##### 错误示例
'''php
if ($condition || false) {
    // 这段代码逻辑不合理，右侧条件总是为假
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
if ($condition || $anotherCondition) {
    // 此代码是合理的，只有当其中一个条件为真时，逻辑块才会执行
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule checks for situations where the logical OR operator consistently returns a false value on the right side. Such situations may indicate a logical error, leading to unexpected behavior in the actual execution of the code.

##### Rule Meaning
Ensure that the use of logical operators is logical, enhancing the correctness and maintainability of the code. Any expression that always returns false may lead to incorrect system states and increase the risk of errors occurring.

##### Error Example
'''php
if ($condition || false) {
    // This code logic is unreasonable; the condition on the right side is always false
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
if ($condition || $anotherCondition) {
    // This code is reasonable; the logical block will only execute if one of the conditions is true
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在逻辑或操作符（`||`）的右侧表达式总是返回真（`true`），这可能会导致条件判断无法正常工作。

##### 规则意义
此规则旨在帮助开发者发现可能的逻辑错误。如果某个条件判断中的逻辑或右侧的表达式始终为真，左侧的任何条件将无效，可能会掩盖潜在的逻辑问题。

##### 错误示例
'''php
$isActive = true;
if ($isActive || true) {
    echo 'This will always execute';
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
$isActive = true;
if ($isActive || false) {
    echo 'This will execute if isActive is true';
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
The expression on the right side of the logical OR operator (`||`) always returns true, which may lead to conditional statements not functioning properly.

##### Rule Meaning
This rule aims to help developers identify potential logical errors. If the expression on the right side of a logical OR in a condition is always true, any condition on the left side will be ineffective, potentially masking underlying logical issues.

##### Error Example
'''php
$isActive = true;
if ($isActive || true) {
    echo 'This will always execute';
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
$isActive = true;
if ($isActive || false) {
    echo 'This will execute if isActive is true';
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在PHP中使用逻辑异或运算符（`xor`）时，如果结果没有被使用，则可能会导致潜在的逻辑错误或不必要的计算。

##### 规则意义
如果一个表达式的结果被计算但没有被使用，可能会导致程序行为不如预期，降低代码质量。开发人员应注意避免将计算结果忽略，以维持代码的可读性和有效性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
$a = true;
$b = false;
// 使用异或运算符，但没有使用结果
$a xor $b;
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
$a = true;
$b = false;
// 使用异或运算符并使用结果
$result = $a xor $b;
if ($result) {
    // 执行某些操作
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
When using the logical XOR operator (`xor`) in PHP, if the result is not utilized, it may lead to potential logical errors or unnecessary computations.

##### Rule Meaning
If the result of an expression is computed but not used, it may cause the program behavior to deviate from expectations, thereby reducing code quality. Developers should be mindful to avoid neglecting the calculated results to maintain code readability and effectiveness.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
$a = true;
$b = false;
// Using the XOR operator, but not utilizing the result
$a xor $b;
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
$a = true;
$b = false;
// Using the XOR operator and utilizing the result
$result = $a xor $b;
if ($result) {
    // Perform some operations
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则检测到在逻辑异或操作符（`xor`）的右侧表达式总是返回 `false` 的情况。

##### 规则意义
使用逻辑异或时，如果右侧表达式总是为假，代码的可读性和逻辑清晰性将受到影响。这种情况可能会导致隐藏的逻辑错误，增加代码维护的复杂度。

##### 错误示例
```php
if ($condition1 xor false) {
    // 执行某些操作
}
```

##### 正确示例
```php
if ($condition1) {
    // 执行某些操作
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule detects cases where the right-side expression of the logical exclusive OR operator (`xor`) always returns `false`.

##### Rule Significance
When using logical exclusive OR, if the right-side expression is always false, it can affect the readability and logical clarity of the code. This situation may lead to hidden logical errors, increasing the complexity of code maintenance.

##### Error Example
```php
if ($condition1 xor false) {
    // 执行某些操作
}
```

##### Correct Example
```php
if ($condition1) {
    // 执行某些操作
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则检查在类外部使用魔术常量（如 `__CLASS__`, `__FILE__` 等）是否符合最佳实践。

##### 规则意义
魔术常量在某些情况下可以提升代码的可读性和维护性，但是在类外部使用这些常量可能导致代码逻辑不清晰，特别是当这些常量所代表的含义无法被树立的上下文所理解时。

##### 错误示例
'''php
<?php
function getClassName() {
    return __CLASS__;
}

getClassName();
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
<?php
class MyClass {
    public function getClassName() {
        return __CLASS__;
    }
}

$instance = new MyClass();
$instance->getClassName();
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule checks whether the use of magic constants (such as `__CLASS__`, `__FILE__`, etc.) outside of classes adheres to best practices.

##### Significance of the Rule
Magic constants can enhance code readability and maintainability in certain situations. However, using these constants outside of classes may lead to unclear code logic, especially when the meaning represented by these constants cannot be understood within the established context.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
<?php
function getClassName() {
    return __CLASS__;
}

getClassName();
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
<?php
class MyClass {
    public function getClassName() {
        return __CLASS__;
    }
}

$instance = new MyClass();
$instance->getClassName();
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
魔术常量（如 `__FILE__`, `__LINE__`, `__DIR__` 等）如果在函数外部使用，可能会导致代码可读性差和意外的行为。

##### 规则意义
确保魔术常量只在函数内部使用，以提高代码的可维护性，同时避免潜在的逻辑错误。

##### 错误示例
'''php
<?php
function doSomething() {
    return __LINE__;
}

echo __LINE__;  // 错误：魔术常量不应用于函数外部
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
<?php
function doSomething() {
    return __LINE__;  // 正确：魔术常量在函数内部使用
}

function anotherFunction() {
    echo doSomething();
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
Magic constants (such as `__FILE__`, `__LINE__`, `__DIR__`, etc.) should not be used outside of functions, as this can lead to poor code readability and unexpected behavior.

##### Rule Significance
Ensure that magic constants are only used within functions to improve code maintainability and avoid potential logic errors.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
<?php
function doSomething() {
    return __LINE__;
}

echo __LINE__;  // Error: Magic constants should not be used outside of functions
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
<?php
function doSomething() {
    return __LINE__;  // Correct: Magic constants are used within the function
}

function anotherFunction() {
    echo doSomething();
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在局部命名空间中使用魔术常量可能导致代码可读性差和意外的行为。

##### 规则意义
在命名空间外部使用魔术常量，例如 `__DIR__`, `__FILE__`, `__NAMESPACE__` 等，可能导致难以追踪的代码错误，特别是在大型项目中。如果不加以注意，可能会引起意想不到的路径问题和名称冲突，从而降低代码的可维护性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
namespace MyNamespace;

function myFunction() {
    // 使用 __FILE__ 获取当前文件路径，但在命名空间外部的情况下使用
    return __FILE__;
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
namespace MyNamespace;

function myFunction() {
    // 访问 __DIR__ 以获取当前命名空间的路径
    return __DIR__ . '/myfile.php';
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
Using magic constants in a local namespace may lead to poor code readability and unexpected behaviors.

##### Rule Meaning
Using magic constants outside of a namespace, such as `__DIR__`, `__FILE__`, `__NAMESPACE__`, etc., can result in difficult-to-trace bugs in the code, especially in large projects. If not carefully managed, it may cause unexpected path issues and name conflicts, thus reducing the maintainability of the code.

##### Error Example
'''php
namespace MyNamespace;

function myFunction() {
    // Using __FILE__ to get the current file path, but in a context outside of the namespace
    return __FILE__;
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
namespace MyNamespace;

function myFunction() {
    // Accessing __DIR__ to get the path of the current namespace
    return __DIR__ . '/myfile.php';
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在PHP的traits中使用魔术常量（如__DIR__、__FILE__等）可能导致意外行为，这是因为它们是相对于使用 trait 的类来解析的。

##### 规则意义
魔术常量的值是根据包含它的上下文来确定的，因此在traits中使用这些常量可能会导致不一致和难以理解的代码行为，从而影响代码的可维护性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
trait ExampleTrait {
    public function getDir() {
        return __DIR__;
    }
}

class Example {
    use ExampleTrait;
}

$example = new Example();
echo $example->getDir(); // 输出的路径与预期不符
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
trait ExampleTrait {
    public function getDir($contextDir) {
        return $contextDir;
    }
}

class Example {
    use ExampleTrait;
    public function showDir() {
        return $this->getDir(__DIR__);
    }
}

$example = new Example();
echo $example->showDir(); // 输出预期路径
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
Using magic constants (such as __DIR__, __FILE__, etc.) in PHP traits may lead to unexpected behavior because they are resolved relative to the class using the trait.

##### Rule Meaning
The value of a magic constant is determined by the context in which it is included, so using these constants in traits can lead to inconsistent and hard-to-understand code behavior, affecting the maintainability of the code.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
trait ExampleTrait {
    public function getDir() {
        return __DIR__;
    }
}

class Example {
    use ExampleTrait;
}

$example = new Example();
echo $example->getDir(); // 输出的路径与预期不符
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
trait ExampleTrait {
    public function getDir($contextDir) {
        return $contextDir;
    }
}

class Example {
    use ExampleTrait;
    public function showDir() {
        return $this->getDir(__DIR__);
    }
}

$example = new Example();
echo $example->showDir(); // 输出预期路径
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在代码中存在无意义的条件语句，这些条件始终返回false。

##### 规则意义
这类条件判断并不会影响程序逻辑，但可能导致代码混乱，并且让其他开发者感到困惑。通过清理这些冗余条件，可以提升代码的可读性和维护性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
if (false) {
    // 这段代码永远不会被执行
    echo "Hello, World!";
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
// 移除无用的条件判断
// echo "Hello, World!";
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
There are meaningless conditional statements in the code that always return false.

##### Rule Meaning
Such conditional checks do not affect the program logic but may lead to code confusion and make other developers feel puzzled. By cleaning up these redundant conditions, the readability and maintainability of the code can be improved.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
if (false) {
    // This code will never be executed
    echo "Hello, World!";
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
// Remove unnecessary conditional checks
// echo "Hello, World!";
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则旨在识别在条件语句中总是返回 `true` 的情况。

##### 规则意义
在条件判断中出现总是返回 `true` 的情况通常意味着代码逻辑存在缺陷，这可能导致不必要的代码执行，降低代码的可读性和可维护性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
if (true) {
    // 这段代码总是会被执行
    echo 'Hello World';
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
$condition = someFunction();
if ($condition) {
    // 仅在 $condition 为 true 时执行
    echo 'Hello World';
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is designed to identify situations where the condition statement always returns `true`.

##### Rule Meaning
The occurrence of an always-returning `true` condition in a conditional statement typically indicates a flaw in the code logic, which may lead to unnecessary code execution and reduce the readability and maintainability of the code.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
if (true) {
    // This code will always be executed
    echo 'Hello World';
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
$condition = someFunction();
if ($condition) {
    // Executes only when $condition is true
    echo 'Hello World';
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则旨在检查代码中是否存在未处理的异常情况。

##### 规则意义
在PHP开发中，未处理的异常可能导致应用程序崩溃或不稳定，增加错误追踪和修复的难度。确保规范处理所有异常可以提升代码的可靠性和用户体验。

##### 错误示例
```php
function divide($a, $b) {
    return $a / $b;
}

divide(5, 0); // 未处理的DivisionByZeroError
```

##### 正确示例
```php
function divide($a, $b) {
    try {
        return $a / $b;
    } catch (DivisionByZeroError $e) {
        return 'Cannot divide by zero'; // 正确处理异常
    }
}

echo divide(5, 0); // 输出: Cannot divide by zero
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule aims to check for unhandled exceptions in the code.

##### Rule Significance
In PHP development, unhandled exceptions can lead to application crashes or instability, making it more difficult to track and fix errors. Ensuring that all exceptions are handled according to standards can enhance code reliability and user experience.

##### Error Example
```php
function divide($a, $b) {
    return $a / $b;
}

divide(5, 0); // Unhandled DivisionByZeroError
```

##### Correct Example
```php
function divide($a, $b) {
    try {
        return $a / $b;
    } catch (DivisionByZeroError $e) {
        return 'Cannot divide by zero'; // Properly handling the exception
    }
}

echo divide(5, 0); // Output: Cannot divide by zero
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则检查函数是否定义为返回值为`void`，并且在实际调用中返回了值。

##### 规则意义
在PHP中，如果一个函数被标记为`void`，则不应返回任何值。返回值可能导致函数调用方的意外行为，并使代码难以理解和维护。

##### 错误示例
'''php
function myFunction(): void {
    return 42; // 错误: 不应返回值
}

myFunction();
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
function myFunction(): void {
    // 正确: 不返回任何值
}

myFunction();
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule checks whether a function is defined to return `void` and returns a value in an actual call.

##### Rule Significance
In PHP, if a function is marked as `void`, it should not return any value. Returning a value may lead to unexpected behavior for the function caller and make the code difficult to understand and maintain.

##### Error Example
'''php
function myFunction(): void {
    return 42; // Error: Should not return a value
}

myFunction();
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
function myFunction(): void {
    // Correct: Does not return any value
}

myFunction();
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则要求所有声明为抽象的方法必须在其父类中被标记为抽象。

##### 规则意义
确保类的设计清晰且符合面向对象编程原则，防止出现实现类没有实现其父类所要求的抽象方法。

##### 错误示例
'''php
abstract class BaseClass {
    abstract protected function myMethod();
}

class ChildClass extends BaseClass {
    protected function myMethod() {
        // 未实现方法
    }
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
abstract class BaseClass {
    abstract protected function myMethod();
}

class ChildClass extends BaseClass {
    protected function myMethod() {
        // 正确实现方法
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule requires that all declared abstract methods must be marked as abstract in their parent classes.

##### Rule Meaning
Ensure that class design is clear and adheres to object-oriented programming principles, preventing the occurrence of implementation classes not implementing the abstract methods required by their parent classes.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
abstract class BaseClass {
    abstract protected function myMethod();
}

class ChildClass extends BaseClass {
    protected function myMethod() {
        // Method not implemented
    }
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
abstract class BaseClass {
    abstract protected function myMethod();
}

class ChildClass extends BaseClass {
    protected function myMethod() {
        // Method implemented correctly
    }
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
当方法返回的类型已经被进一步限制时，不应重复创建这种类型。此规则旨在防止不必要的类型限制代码，从而提高代码的可读性和维护性。

##### 规则意义
在 PHP 中，类型系统允许使用更具体的类型来增强代码的清晰度和安全性。但是，如果在类的方法中多次使用已经边界限制的类型，可能会导致代码冗余和可读性下降。

##### 错误示例
'''php
class Example {
    /**
     * @param string $input
     * @return string
     */
    public function process(string $input): string {
        return $input;
    }

    /**
     * @param mixed $input
     * @return string
     */
    public function handle($input): string {
        return $this->process($input);
    }
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
class Example {
    /**
     * @param string $input
     * @return string
     */
    public function process(string $input): string {
        return $input;
    }

    /**
     * @param string $input
     * @return string
     */
    public function handle(string $input): string {
        return $this->process($input);
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
Types that have already been further constrained by the method should not be redefined. This rule aims to prevent unnecessary type constraint code, thereby improving code readability and maintainability.

##### Rule Significance
In PHP, the type system allows for the use of more specific types to enhance code clarity and safety. However, if already constrained types are used multiple times within class methods, it can lead to code redundancy and decreased readability.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
class Example {
    /**
     * @param string $input
     * @return string
     */
    public function process(string $input): string {
        return $input;
    }

    /**
     * @param mixed $input
     * @return string
     */
    public function handle($input): string {
        return $this->process($input);
    }
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
class Example {
    /**
     * @param string $input
     * @return string
     */
    public function process(string $input): string {
        return $input;
    }

    /**
     * @param string $input
     * @return string
     */
    public function handle(string $input): string {
        return $this->process($input);
    }
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在 PHP 中，调用一个抽象类的方法是不可行的，因此不应该在具体实现中直接使用抽象方法。

##### 规则意义
调用抽象方法可能导致不可预期的行为，以及运行时错误。遵循此规则可以确保代码的可维护性和可靠性，防止潜在的错误。

##### 错误示例
'''php
abstract class AbstractClass {
    abstract public function doSomething();
}

class ConcreteClass extends AbstractClass {
    public function execute() {
        // 错误：不能调用抽象方法
        $this->doSomething();
    }
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
abstract class AbstractClass {
    abstract public function doSomething();
}

class ConcreteClass extends AbstractClass {
    public function doSomething() {
        // 正确的实现
        echo 'Doing something';
    }

    public function execute() {
        // 正确：调用实现的方法
        $this->doSomething();
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In PHP, it is not possible to call a method of an abstract class, and therefore, abstract methods should not be directly used in concrete implementations.

##### Rule Meaning
Calling abstract methods may lead to unpredictable behavior and runtime errors. Adhering to this rule ensures the maintainability and reliability of the code, preventing potential errors.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
abstract class AbstractClass {
    abstract public function doSomething();
}

class ConcreteClass extends AbstractClass {
    public function execute() {
        // Error: cannot call abstract method
        $this->doSomething();
    }
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
abstract class AbstractClass {
    abstract public function doSomething();
}

class ConcreteClass extends AbstractClass {
    public function doSomething() {
        // Correct implementation
        echo 'Doing something';
    }

    public function execute() {
        // Correct: calling the implemented method
        $this->doSomething();
    }
}
'''

