}

class ChildClass extends ParentClass {
    public function getInstance(): ParentClass { // 错误：返回类型不匹配
        return new ParentClass();
    }
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
class ParentClass {
    public function getInstance(): ParentClass {
        return new ParentClass();
    }
}

class ChildClass extends ParentClass {
    public function getInstance(): ChildClass { // 正确：返回类型一致
        return new ChildClass();
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule requires that the return type of a method should match the return type of its subclass to ensure type consistency and predictability.

##### Rule Meaning
Type consistency can improve code maintainability and readability. Especially in object-oriented programming, polymorphism relies on matching the types of method return values. Adhering to this rule can reduce potential type errors and ensure that callers have a clear expectation when using the return values.

##### Error Example
'''php
class ParentClass {
    public function getInstance(): ChildClass {
        return new ChildClass();
    }
}

class ChildClass extends ParentClass {
    public function getInstance(): ParentClass { // Error: return type mismatch
        return new ParentClass();
    }
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
class ParentClass {
    public function getInstance(): ParentClass {
        return new ParentClass();
    }
}

class ChildClass extends ParentClass {
    public function getInstance(): ChildClass { // Correct: return type matches
        return new ChildClass();
    }
}
'''

