}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则旨在检测在代码中使用动态方法名的情况，即通过变量或字符串动态调用方法，这可能导致代码的可读性和维护性降低。

##### 规则意义
使用动态方法名会使得代码难以追踪和理解，特别是在大型项目中，可能会导致错误的调用或安全问题。推荐使用静态方法名以提高代码的可读性。建议将动态调用替换为显式的方法调用。 

##### 错误示例
'''php
class Example {
    public function hello() {
        return "Hello, World!";
    }

    public function callMethod($methodName) {
        return $this->$methodName(); // 动态方法调用
    }
}

$example = new Example();
echo $example->callMethod('hello');
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
class Example {
    public function hello() {
        return "Hello, World!";
    }

    public function callHello() {
        return $this->hello(); // 静态方式调用
    }
}

$example = new Example();
echo $example->callHello();
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule aims to detect the use of dynamic method names in the code, which involves dynamically invoking methods through variables or strings, potentially reducing code readability and maintainability.

##### Significance of the Rule
Using dynamic method names can make code difficult to trace and understand, especially in large projects, and may lead to erroneous calls or security issues. It is recommended to use static method names to improve code readability. It is advised to replace dynamic calls with explicit method calls.

##### Error Example
'''php
class Example {
    public function hello() {
        return "Hello, World!";
    }

    public function callMethod($methodName) {
        return $this->$methodName(); // Dynamic method call
    }
}

$example = new Example();
echo $example->callMethod('hello');
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
class Example {
    public function hello() {
        return "Hello, World!";
    }

    public function callHello() {
        return $this->hello(); // Static method call
    }
}

$example = new Example();
echo $example->callHello();
'''

