rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则检查类中的方法是否标记为抽象方法，确保类的方法实现完整。

##### 规则意义
类在使用时应该具备完整的方法实现，抽象方法使得类不具备直接实例化的能力。这样可以避免在编码时遇到未实现方法的问题，提升代码的可维护性和可读性。

##### 错误示例
```php
abstract class BaseClass {
    abstract public function doSomething();
}
class ConcreteClass extends BaseClass {
    // 方法未实现，导致类不可用。
}
```

##### 正确示例
```php
class ConcreteClass {
    public function doSomething() {
        // 方法实现逻辑。
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule checks whether methods in a class are marked as abstract methods, ensuring that the class has complete method implementations.

##### Rule Significance
Classes should have complete method implementations when being used. Abstract methods prevent classes from being instantiated directly. This helps avoid issues with unimplemented methods during coding, enhancing the maintainability and readability of the code.

##### Error Example
```php
abstract class BaseClass {
    abstract public function doSomething();
}
class ConcreteClass extends BaseClass {
    // Method not implemented, making the class unusable.
}
```

##### Correct Example
