    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则旨在检测在方法定义中不使用对象类型，提醒开发者在必要的情况下使用对象，使代码更具可读性和可维护性。

##### 规则意义
在PHP中，使用对象可以提高代码的可读性和模块化。方法如果定义为接受某个对象作为参数，而实际传入了其他类型，可能导致不可预测的错误。

##### 错误示例
'''php
class Example {
    public function process($data) {
        // 处理数据
    }
}
$example = new Example();
$example->process("string data"); // 错误：传入了非对象类型
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
class Example {
    public function process(SomeObject $data) {
        // 处理数据
    }
}
$example = new Example();
$example->process(new SomeObject()); // 正确：传入了对象类型
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule aims to detect the failure to use object types in method definitions and reminds developers to utilize objects when necessary, enhancing the readability and maintainability of the code.

##### Rule Meaning
In PHP, using objects can improve code readability and modularity. If a method is defined to accept an object as a parameter but a different type is actually passed in, it can lead to unpredictable errors.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
class Example {
    public function process($data) {
        // Process data
    }
}
$example = new Example();
$example->process("string data"); // Error: non-object type passed in
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
class Example {
    public function process(SomeObject $data) {
        // Process data
    }
}
$example = new Example();
$example->process(new SomeObject()); // Correct: object type passed in
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在类中调用非静态方法时，确保该方法必须是通过实例访问而不是静态访问。

##### 规则意义
采用非静态方法是一种面向对象编程的实践，确保方法能够访问类的状态和属性。错误地调用非静态方法为静态方法带来了不必要的复杂性，可能导致程序逻辑错误。

##### 错误示例
```php
class MyClass {
    public function myMethod() {
        return 'Hello';
    }
}

// 错误：尝试以静态方式调用非静态方法
$result = MyClass::myMethod();
```

##### 正确示例
```php
class MyClass {
    public function myMethod() {
        return 'Hello';
    }
}

// 正确：通过类的实例调用非静态方法
$instance = new MyClass();
$result = $instance->myMethod();
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
When calling a non-static method in a class, ensure that the method is accessed through an instance and not statically.

##### Rule Meaning
Using non-static methods is an object-oriented programming practice that ensures methods can access the state and properties of the class. Incorrectly calling a non-static method as if it were static introduces unnecessary complexity and can lead to logical errors in the program.

##### Incorrect Example
```php
class MyClass {
    public function myMethod() {
        return 'Hello';
    }
}

// Incorrect: Attempting to call a non-static method statically
$result = MyClass::myMethod();
```

##### Correct Example
```php
class MyClass {
    public function myMethod() {
        return 'Hello';
    }
}

// Correct: Calling a non-static method through an instance of the class
$instance = new MyClass();
$result = $instance->myMethod();
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则检查代码中调用的方法是否存在。如果调用的方法未定义，将导致运行时错误。

##### 规则意义
确保调用的方法在当前上下文中是有效的，有助于提高代码的稳定性和可预测性，避免在运行时遇到未定义方法的错误。

##### 错误示例
'''php
class MyClass {
    public function doSomething() {
        $this->undefinedMethod(); // 这里调用了未定义的方法
    }
}
$instance = new MyClass();
$instance->doSomething();
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
class MyClass {
    public function doSomething() {
        $this->definedMethod(); // 调用已定义的方法
    }

    public function definedMethod() {
        // 方法的实现
    }
}
$instance = new MyClass();
$instance->doSomething();
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule checks whether the method being called in the code exists. Calling an undefined method will lead to a runtime error.

##### Rule Significance
Ensuring that the called method is valid in the current context helps improve the stability and predictability of the code, preventing errors due to undefined methods at runtime.

##### Error Example
'''php
class MyClass {
    public function doSomething() {
        $this->undefinedMethod(); // Calling an undefined method here
    }
}
$instance = new MyClass();
$instance->doSomething();
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
class MyClass {
    public function doSomething() {
        $this->definedMethod(); // Calling a defined method
    }

    public function definedMethod() {
        // Implementation of the method
    }
}
$instance = new MyClass();
$instance->doSomething();
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在类的子类中重写父类的方法时，建议使用`parent::methodName()`调用父类的方法。未能正确重写的方法可能导致意外的行为。

##### 规则意义
确保在重写方法时，能够维持父类的逻辑和状态，避免意外覆盖原有功能，增强代码的可维护性和可读性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
class ParentClass {
    public function someMethod() {
        // 一些逻辑
    }
}

class ChildClass extends ParentClass {
    public function someMethod() {
        // 不调用父类的方法，可能导致逻辑缺失
    }
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
class ParentClass {
    public function someMethod() {
        // 一些逻辑
    }
}

class ChildClass extends ParentClass {
    public function someMethod() {
        // 先调用父类的方法
        parent::someMethod();
        // 子类中扩展逻辑
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
When overriding a method from the parent class in a subclass, it is recommended to use `parent::methodName()` to call the parent class method. Failing to properly override the method may result in unexpected behavior.

##### Rule Significance
Ensuring that the logic and state of the parent class are maintained when overriding methods helps to avoid unintentionally overriding existing functionality, enhancing the maintainability and readability of the code.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
class ParentClass {
    public function someMethod() {
        // Some logic
    }
}

class ChildClass extends ParentClass {
    public function someMethod() {
        // Not calling the parent method may lead to logic loss
    }
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
class ParentClass {
    public function someMethod() {
        // Some logic
    }
}

class ChildClass extends ParentClass {
    public function someMethod() {
        // Call the parent method first
        parent::someMethod();
        // Extend logic in the subclass
    }
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
当在子类中重写父类的方法时，如果父类的方法声明为`final`，则不允许重写该方法。

##### 规则意义
确保遵循面向对象编程原则，避免子类无意中重写不应被重写的方法，保持代码的一致性和可维护性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
class ParentClass {
    final public function finalMethod() {
        // 方法实现
    }
}

class ChildClass extends ParentClass {
    public function finalMethod() {
        // 试图重写final方法
    }
}
''' 

##### 正确示例
'''php
class ParentClass {
    final public function finalMethod() {
        // 方法实现
    }
}

class ChildClass extends ParentClass {
    public function someOtherMethod() {
        // 正确，不重写final方法
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
When overriding a method from a parent class in a subclass, if the parent class method is declared as `final`, it is not permissible to override that method.

##### Rule Significance
Ensure adherence to object-oriented programming principles, preventing subclasses from unintentionally overriding methods that should not be overridden, and maintaining code consistency and maintainability.

##### Error Example
'''php
class ParentClass {
    final public function finalMethod() {
        // 方法实现
    }
}

class ChildClass extends ParentClass {
    public function finalMethod() {
        // 试图重写final方法
    }
}
''' 

 ##### Correct Example
'''php
class ParentClass {
    final public function finalMethod() {
        // 方法实现
    }
}

class ChildClass extends ParentClass {
    public function someOtherMethod() {
        // 正确，不重写final方法
    }
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
当在子类中尝试重写一个在父类中被标记为 `final` 的方法时，代码将产生错误。这个规则确保开发人员遵循面向对象编程的原则，避免意外重写不应修改的方法。

##### 规则意义
保证类的设计合理性，避免不必要的运行时错误和逻辑混乱。重写 `final` 方法是一种不恰当的行为，因为 `final` 方法已经被声明为不可重写，这意味着父类的设计者期望这个方法的实现不可被改变。

##### 错误示例
```php
class ParentClass {
    final public function doSomething() {
        echo 'Doing something';
    }
}

class ChildClass extends ParentClass {
    public function doSomething() {
        echo 'Trying to override';
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```php
class ParentClass {
    final public function doSomething() {
        echo 'Doing something';
    }
}

class ChildClass extends ParentClass {
    // 不重写final方法，遵循设计
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
When attempting to override a method in a subclass that has been marked as `final` in the parent class, an error will occur. This rule ensures that developers adhere to the principles of object-oriented programming, avoiding accidental overrides of methods that should not be modified.

##### Rule Significance
Ensures the rationality of class design, avoiding unnecessary runtime errors and logical confusion. Overriding a `final` method is an inappropriate behavior because `final` methods have been declared as non-overrideable, which means that the designer of the parent class expects the implementation of this method to remain unchanged.

##### Error Example
```php
class ParentClass {
    final public function doSomething() {
        echo 'Doing something';
    }
}

class ChildClass extends ParentClass {
    public function doSomething() {
        echo 'Trying to override';
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```php
class ParentClass {
    final public function doSomething() {
        echo 'Doing something';
    }
}

class ChildClass extends ParentClass {
    // Do not override final method, adhere to design
}
```

