#### 规则概述
本规则要求类的方法如果是静态的，应该被标记为`static`。

##### 规则意义
静态方法属于类本身而不是类的实例，标记为`static`可以提高代码的可读性，并避免不必要的实例化开销。同时，静态方法无法访问类的非静态属性和方法，从而提高代码的清晰度。

##### 错误示例
'''php
class Example {
    public function doSomething() {
        // ...
    }
}

$example = new Example();
$example->doSomething();
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
class Example {
    public static function doSomething() {
        // ...
    }
}

Example::doSomething();
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule requires that if a method in a class is static, it should be marked as `static`.

##### Rule Significance
Static methods belong to the class itself rather than to instances of the class. Marking them as `static` can improve code readability and avoid unnecessary instantiation overhead. Additionally, static methods cannot access non-static properties and methods of the class, enhancing code clarity.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
class Example {
    public function doSomething() {
        // ...
    }
}

$example = new Example();
$example->doSomething();
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
class Example {
    public static function doSomething() {
        // ...
    }
}

Example::doSomething();
'''

