rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则检查函数参数或返回值中缺失的可调用类型声明，以确保可读性和代码安全性。

##### 规则意义
在PHP中，使用可调用类型可以帮助开发者明确一个函数期望接收的回调类型，从而减少潜在的运行时错误，提高代码的可维护性与可读性。当未明确指定类型时，可能导致不必要的错误和难以追踪的问题。

##### 错误示例
'''php
function executeCallback($callback) {
    // 执行回调
    $callback();
}

executeCallback('not_a_function'); // 这里导致了运行时错误
''' 

##### 正确示例
'''php
function executeCallback(callable $callback) {
    // 执行回调
    $callback();
}

executeCallback(function() {
    echo 'This is a valid callback';
});
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule checks for missing callable type declarations in function parameters or return values to ensure readability and code safety.

##### Rule Significance
In PHP, using callable types helps developers specify the expected callback type that a function will receive, thereby reducing potential runtime errors and improving the maintainability and readability of the code. When types are not explicitly defined, it can lead to unnecessary errors and hard-to-trace issues.

##### Error Example
'''php
function executeCallback($callback) {
    // Execute callback
    $callback();
}

executeCallback('not_a_function'); // This causes a runtime error
''' 

##### Correct Example
'''php
function executeCallback(callable $callback) {
    // Execute callback
    $callback();
}

executeCallback(function() {
    echo 'This is a valid callback';
});
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在函数或方法中，如果抛出检查异常而没有明确指定其类型，则会导致代码的可读性和可维护性下降。

##### 规则意义
明确声明方法抛出的检查异常类型可以使得代码更加清晰，便于使用者理解潜在的错误，并进行正确的错误处理。缺少类型的检查异常可能导致开发者在捕获异常时无从处理，造成潜在的bug或系统崩溃。

##### 错误示例
'''php
class Example {
    public function doSomething() {
        // 这里抛出了一个检查异常，但没有指明其类型
        throw new Exception('Something went wrong!');
    }
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
class Example {
    public function doSomething() : void {
        // 明确声明了可能抛出的检查异常
        throw new untimeException('Something went wrong!');
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In functions or methods, throwing a checked exception without explicitly specifying its type leads to decreased readability and maintainability of the code.

##### Significance of the Rule
Explicitly declaring the types of checked exceptions that a method can throw makes the code clearer, allowing users to understand potential errors and handle them correctly. Lack of type information for checked exceptions may leave developers unsure how to handle exceptions when caught, resulting in potential bugs or system crashes.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
class Example {
    public function doSomething() {
        // A checked exception is thrown here, but its type is not specified
        throw new Exception('Something went wrong!');
    }
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
class Example {
    public function doSomething() : void {
        // The potential checked exception is explicitly declared
        throw new RuntimeException('Something went wrong!');
    }
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
当使用数组或集合时，没有提供泛型类型定义会导致类型不明确，增加潜在的错误风险。

##### 规则意义
确保在使用泛型集合时提供具体的类型定义，以提高代码的可读性和可维护性，减少运行时错误。

##### 错误示例
'''php
function getItems(array $items) {
    foreach ($items as $item) {
        // 对于$item的类型没有明确规定
    }
}

getItems(['a', 1, true]); // 传递不同类型的数据
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
function getItems(array $items) : array {
    foreach ($items as $item) {
        // 假设我们要求传入的类型为字符串
        // 在此明确类型
        assert(is_string($item)); // 增加类型检查
    }
    return $items;
}

getItems(['a', 'b', 'c']); // 传递相同类型的数据
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
When using arrays or collections, failing to provide a generic type definition can lead to unclear types and increase the risk of potential errors.

##### Rule Significance
Ensure that a specific type definition is provided when using generic collections to enhance code readability and maintainability, reducing runtime errors.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
function getItems(array $items) {
    foreach ($items as $item) {
        // The type of $item is not explicitly defined
    }
}

getItems(['a', 1, true]); // Passing different types of data
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
function getItems(array $items) : array {
    foreach ($items as $item) {
        // Assume we require the input type to be string
        // Explicitly define the type here
        assert(is_string($item)); // Add type check
    }
    return $items;
}

getItems(['a', 'b', 'c']); // Passing the same type of data
'''

rules.content:
