This rule detects situations in the code where an inequality comparison always returns true, which may lead to logical errors.

##### Significance of the Rule
In business logic, when using inequality comparisons, it is essential to ensure that the conditions can be correctly evaluated. Inequality comparisons that always return true can lead to potential errors, requiring developers to review the code logic.

##### Error Example
