rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule requires PHP classes to explicitly implement all methods of the interface when implementing it.

##### Rule Significance
If a class implementing an interface does not implement all the methods in the interface, it may lead to runtime errors, affecting the stability and maintainability of the program. By adhering to this rule, we can ensure the correctness of the class and its consistency with the interface.

##### Error Example
'''php
interface ExampleInterface {
    public function exampleMethod();
}

class ExampleClass implements ExampleInterface {
    // Missing implementation of exampleMethod
}
''' 

##### Correct Example
'''php
interface ExampleInterface {
    public function exampleMethod();
}

class ExampleClass implements ExampleInterface {
    public function exampleMethod() {
        // Implementation here
    }
}
'''

