rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则检测函数的返回值是否为空，以避免不必要的错误和不确定性。

##### 规则意义
对于需要返回值的函数，如果未正确返回值，将导致调用者收到不明确的结果。确保函数始终返回有效的数据对于提高代码的可靠性和可维护性至关重要。

##### 错误示例
```php
function getUser($id) {
    // ... 进行一些操作
}

$user = getUser(1);
// $user 可能为 null，这样会导致后续操作失败
```

##### 正确示例
```php
function getUser($id) {
    // ... 进行一些操作
    return $user; // 确保返回一个用户对象或有效的返回值
}

$user = getUser(1);
// $user 应始终是一个有效的用户对象
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule detects whether the return value of a function is empty to avoid unnecessary errors and uncertainty.

##### Rule Meaning
For functions that need to return a value, failing to return a value correctly will result in the caller receiving an ambiguous result. Ensuring that functions always return valid data is crucial for improving code reliability and maintainability.

##### Error Example
```php
function getUser($id) {
    // ... perform some operations
}

$user = getUser(1);
// $user may be null, which could cause subsequent operations to fail
```

##### Correct Example
```php
function getUser($id) {
    // ... perform some operations
    return $user; // Ensure to return a user object or a valid return value
}

$user = getUser(1);
// $user should always be a valid user object
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则检测函数在所有代码路径中是否都有返回值。

##### 规则意义
缺失的返回值可能会导致函数不可预测的行为，这使得代码更容易出错，尤其是在需要根据返回值进行后续操作的情况下。确保函数在所有可执行路径上都有明确的返回值，可以提高代码的可靠性和可读性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
function calculate($a, $b) {
    if ($a > $b) {
        return $a;
    }
    // 缺少else条件下的返回值
}

$result = calculate(3, 2);  // 可能会产生未定义的行为
''' 

##### 正确示例
'''php
function calculate($a, $b) {
    if ($a > $b) {
        return $a;
    } else {
        return $b;
    }
}

$result = calculate(3, 2);  // 总是有返回值，代码可预测
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule detects whether a function has a return value in all code paths.

##### Rule Meaning
Missing return values can lead to unpredictable behavior in functions, making the code more error-prone, especially in cases where subsequent operations depend on the return value. Ensuring that functions have a clear return value on all executable paths can enhance the reliability and readability of the code.

##### Error Example
'''php
function calculate($a, $b) {
    if ($a > $b) {
        return $a;
    }
    // Missing return value in the else condition
}

$result = calculate(3, 2);  // May produce undefined behavior
''' 

##### Correct Example
'''php
function calculate($a, $b) {
    if ($a > $b) {
        return $a;
    } else {
        return $b;
    }
}

$result = calculate(3, 2);  // Always has a return value, code is predictable
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在函数或方法中，返回值不应为null，特别是在接口设计中，这可能导致调用方出现意料之外的错误。

##### 规则意义
保证函数总是返回有效值，避免因返回null而在后续处理中引发错误，增强代码的健壮性和可维护性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
function fetchData($id) {
    if ($id <= 0) {
        return null; // 返回null，可能导致意外错误
    }
    return 'data';
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
function fetchData($id) {
    if ($id <= 0) {
        throw new InvalidArgumentException('Invalid ID provided'); // 抛出异常而不是返回null
    }
    return 'data';
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In functions or methods, return values should not be null, especially in interface design, as this may lead to unexpected errors for the caller.

##### Rule Meaning
Ensure that functions always return valid values to avoid errors in subsequent processing due to returning null, enhancing the robustness and maintainability of the code.

##### Error Example
'''php
function fetchData($id) {
    if ($id <= 0) {
        return null; // Returning null may lead to unexpected errors
    }
    return 'data';
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
function fetchData($id) {
    if ($id <= 0) {
        throw new InvalidArgumentException('Invalid ID provided'); // Throw an exception instead of returning null
    }
    return 'data';
}
'''

rules.content:
