rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则用于捕捉在静态方法中调用抽象方法的情况。

##### 规则意义
在PHP中，抽象方法必须在子类中实现，而静态方法是与类相关的，不应该在父类中直接调用抽象方法。这会导致运行时错误，影响代码的可维护性和稳定性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
abstract class BaseClass {
    abstract protected function doSomething();

    public static function callAbstractMethod() {
        // 错误：在静态方法中调用抽象方法
        return $this->doSomething();
    }
}

class ChildClass extends BaseClass {
    protected function doSomething() {
        return 'Done';
    }
}

BaseClass::callAbstractMethod(); // 运行时错误
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
abstract class BaseClass {
    abstract protected function doSomething();

    public function callMethod() {
        // 正确：使用实例方法来调用抽象方法
        return $this->doSomething();
    }
}

class ChildClass extends BaseClass {
    protected function doSomething() {
        return 'Done';
    }
}

$instance = new ChildClass();
$instance->callMethod(); // 输出 'Done'
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is used to capture the situation of calling an abstract method within a static method.

##### Rule Meaning
In PHP, abstract methods must be implemented in subclasses, and static methods are associated with the class and should not directly call abstract methods in the parent class. This can lead to runtime errors, affecting the maintainability and stability of the code.

##### Error Example
'''php
abstract class BaseClass {
    abstract protected function doSomething();

    public static function callAbstractMethod() {
        // Error: Calling an abstract method within a static method
        return $this->doSomething();
    }
}

class ChildClass extends BaseClass {
    protected function doSomething() {
        return 'Done';
    }
}

BaseClass::callAbstractMethod(); // Runtime error
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
abstract class BaseClass {
    abstract protected function doSomething();

    public function callMethod() {
        // Correct: Using an instance method to call the abstract method
        return $this->doSomething();
    }
}

class ChildClass extends BaseClass {
    protected function doSomething() {
        return 'Done';
    }
}

$instance = new ChildClass();
$instance->callMethod(); // Outputs 'Done'
'''

