rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在Symfony框架中，私有服务不应在外部直接访问，这是为了确保服务的封装性和依赖注入的正确使用。

##### 规则意义
使用私有服务可能导致不可预期的错误和维护问题，降低代码的可读性与可测试性。建议在控制器或其它服务中通过构造函数注入所需的依赖，避免直接创建或访问私有服务。

##### 错误示例
'''php
// 错误代码示例：直接在控制器中使用私有服务
$container->get('my_private_service');
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
// 正确代码示例：通过构造函数注入服务
class MyController {
    private $myPrivateService;

    public function __construct(MyPrivateService $myPrivateService) {
        $this->myPrivateService = $myPrivateService;
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In the Symfony framework, private services should not be accessed directly from outside, in order to ensure service encapsulation and the proper use of dependency injection.

##### Significance of the Rule
Using private services can lead to unexpected errors and maintenance issues, reducing code readability and testability. It is recommended to inject required dependencies through the constructor in controllers or other services, avoiding the direct creation or access of private services.

##### Error Example
'''php
// Error code example: directly using a private service inside a controller
$container->get('my_private_service');
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
// Correct code example: injecting the service through the constructor
class MyController {
    private $myPrivateService;

    public function __construct(MyPrivateService $myPrivateService) {
        $this->myPrivateService = $myPrivateService;
    }
}
'''

