    use MyTrait, 'SomeUnexpectedTrait'; // 错误：使用了不在枚举内的trait
}
```

##### 正确示例
```php
enum SupportedTraits {
    case MyTrait;
}

trait MyTrait {
    public function doSomething() {}
}

class MyClass {
    use MyTrait;
}

class AnotherClass {
    use MyTrait;
}

class CorrectClass {
    use SupportedTraits::MyTrait; // 正确：使用了明确的枚举
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In PHP, traits allow classes to share functionality, often used for code reuse. However, in certain cases, it is important to use enums to ensure that the usage of traits is more explicit and safe.

##### Significance of the Rule
Using enums to define and restrict the use of traits can reduce potential errors and improve code maintainability. Doing so ensures that the application of traits adheres to expected behavior and makes the code logic clearer.

##### Incorrect Example
```php
trait MyTrait {
    public function doSomething() {}
}

class MyClass {
    use MyTrait;
}

class AnotherClass {
    use MyTrait;
}

class IncorrectClass {
    use MyTrait, 'SomeUnexpectedTrait'; // Error: using a trait not in the enum
}
```

##### Correct Example
```php
enum SupportedTraits {
    case MyTrait;
}

trait MyTrait {
    public function doSomething() {}
}

class MyClass {
    use MyTrait;
}

class AnotherClass {
    use MyTrait;
}

class CorrectClass {
    use SupportedTraits::MyTrait; // Correct: using an explicit enum
}
```

