rules.content:
#### 规则概述
联合类型是PHP 8引入的一种特性，允许开发者声明一个值可能是多种类型之一。然而，在使用mixed类型作为联合类型的一部分时，可能会导致代码的可维护性和可读性降低。

##### 规则意义
使用mixed类型会使得值的类型不明确，可能导致潜在的错误和不一致性。为了提高代码质量，我们建议避免在联合类型中使用mixed。

##### 错误示例
```php
function processValue(int|string $value): void {
    // 假设此处value应为整型或字符串，混合使用会导致不确定性
    if (is_string($value)) {
        echo "Value is a string: " . $value;
    } else {
        echo "Value is an integer: " . $value;
    }
}

function example(mixed $input): void {
    processValue($input); // 使用mixed作为类型，影响processValue的调用
}
```

##### 正确示例
```php
function processValue(int|string $value): void {
    if (is_string($value)) {
        echo "Value is a string: " . $value;
    } else {
        echo "Value is an integer: " . $value;
    }
}

function example(int|string $input): void {
    processValue($input); // 明确类型，增强类型安全性
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
Union types are a feature introduced in PHP 8 that allow developers to declare that a value can be one of several types. However, using mixed types as part of a union type may reduce the maintainability and readability of the code.

##### Rule Significance
Using mixed types makes the type of a value unclear, which can lead to potential errors and inconsistencies. To improve code quality, we recommend avoiding the use of mixed in union types.

##### Error Example
```php
function processValue(int|string $value): void {
    // Assuming value here should be either an integer or a string, mixing them causes uncertainty
    if (is_string($value)) {
        echo "Value is a string: " . $value;
    } else {
        echo "Value is an integer: " . $value;
    }
}

function example(mixed $input): void {
    processValue($input); // Using mixed as a type affects the call to processValue
}
```

##### Correct Example
```php
function processValue(int|string $value): void {
    if (is_string($value)) {
        echo "Value is a string: " . $value;
    } else {
        echo "Value is an integer: " . $value;
    }
}

function example(int|string $input): void {
    processValue($input); // Explicit types enhance type safety
}
```

rules.content:
