rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在 PHP 中，使用 `unset` 函数时，如果尝试解除一个对象的钩子属性，可能会导致预期外的行为。

##### 规则意义
确保在使用 `unset` 函数时，您不会意外解除对象的钩子属性，这可能导致属性状态不一致或对象行为异常。

##### 错误示例
```php
class Example {
    public $hookedProperty;
    public function __construct() {
        $this->hookedProperty = 'initial';
    }
}

$instance = new Example();

// 错误：尝试解除钩子属性
unset($instance->hookedProperty);
```

##### 正确示例
```php
class Example {
    public $property;
    public $hookedProperty;
    public function __construct() {
        $this->property = 'initial';
        $this->hookedProperty = 'hooked';
    }
}

$instance = new Example();

// 正确：只解除常规属性
unset($instance->property);
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In PHP, when using the `unset` function, attempting to unset a hook property of an object may lead to unexpected behavior.

##### Rule Meaning
Ensure that when using the `unset` function, you do not accidentally unset a hook property of an object, as this can lead to inconsistent property states or abnormal object behavior.

##### Error Example
```php
class Example {
    public $hookedProperty;
    public function __construct() {
        $this->hookedProperty = 'initial';
    }
}

$instance = new Example();

// Error: attempting to unset hook property
unset($instance->hookedProperty);
```

##### Correct Example
```php
class Example {
    public $property;
    public $hookedProperty;
    public function __construct() {
        $this->property = 'initial';
        $this->hookedProperty = 'hooked';
    }
}

$instance = new Example();

// Correct: only unsetting a regular property
unset($instance->property);
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
当使用`unset`删除一个对象的属性时，如果该属性可能通过魔术方法（如`__get`和`__set`）被钩子干扰，可能会导致代码的不稳定或难以理解。建议在删除属性前检查其使用情况。

##### 规则意义
未恰当地使用`unset`可能导致意想不到的行为，特别是在涉及使用魔术方法的类中。这种情况可能会在运行时引入错误，或者影响对象的预期状态，最终导致代码的质量降低。

##### 错误示例
```php
class MyClass {
    private $property;

    public function __get($name) {
        return $this->property;
    }

    public function __set($name, $value) {
        $this->property = $value;
    }
}

$obj = new MyClass();
$obj->someProperty = 'value';
unset($obj->someProperty); // 可能导致未预期的行为
```

##### 正确示例
```php
class MyClass {
    private $property;

    public function __get($name) {
        return $this->property;
    }

    public function __set($name, $value) {
        $this->property = $value;
    }
}

$obj = new MyClass();
$obj->someProperty = 'value';
// 先确保不再需要该属性的使用，然后再进行unset操作
if (isset($obj->someProperty)) {
    unset($obj->someProperty);
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
When using `unset` to delete a property of an object, if that property could be interfered with by magic methods (such as `__get` and `__set`), it may lead to unstable or hard-to-understand code. It is recommended to check the usage of the property before deleting it.

##### Rule Meaning
Improper use of `unset` can lead to unexpected behavior, especially in classes that involve magic methods. This situation may introduce errors at runtime or affect the expected state of the object, ultimately reducing the quality of the code.

##### Error Example
```php
class MyClass {
