rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule prohibits the unset operation on a read-only property to avoid undefined behavior.

##### Rule Significance
The design intention of read-only properties is to protect the integrity and consistency of the data. Performing an unset operation on these properties may lead to unexpected behavior in the program, introducing errors or vulnerabilities.

##### Error Example
'''php
class User {
    private $name;
    private $readonlyProp;

    public function __construct($name) {
        $this->name = $name;
        $this->readonlyProp = 'This is read-only';
