#### 规则概述
此规则用于检测在PHP中返回类型为`void`的函数是否符合纯粹性标准。

##### 规则意义
纯粹的`void`函数不应产生任何副作用，应当只依赖其输入参数。确保函数没有改变任何外部状态，便于提高代码的可测试性与可维护性。

##### 错误示例
'''php
function updateValue(&$value) {
    $value = 5; // 修改了外部状态
}

function voidFunction(): void {
    updateValue($value); // 调用非纯函数
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''php
function calculateSum(int $a, int $b): int {
    return $a + $b; // 纯函数，没有副作用
}

function voidFunction(): void {
    $result = calculateSum(3, 2); // 只依赖输入，无副作用
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is used to detect whether functions in PHP that have a return type of `void` meet the purity standards.

##### Rule Meaning
A pure `void` function should not produce any side effects and should only rely on its input parameters. Ensuring that the function does not change any external state helps improve the testability and maintainability of the code.

##### Incorrect Example
'''php
function updateValue(&$value) {
    $value = 5; // Modifies external state
}

function voidFunction(): void {
    updateValue($value); // Calls a non-pure function
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''php
function calculateSum(int $a, int $b): int {
    return $a + $b; // Pure function, no side effects
}

function voidFunction(): void {
    $result = calculateSum(3, 2); // Only depends on input, no side effects
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则检查在while循环中是否有条件恒为false的情况。

##### 规则意义
无条件的while循环可能导致无限循环，或者循环体永远不执行，这会导致程序错误或性能问题。确保循环条件是动态的或有效的，可以减少潜在的逻辑错误。

##### 错误示例
'''php
while (false) {
    echo "这段代码永远不会执行";
}

while (1 === 1) {
    // 这段代码会导致无限循环
}
'''\n
##### 正确示例
'''php
$condition = true;
while ($condition) {
    echo "这段代码会在条件为真时执行";
    // 更新条件以避免无限循环
    $condition = false;
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule checks for conditions that are always false in a while loop.

##### Rule Meaning
Unconditional while loops can lead to infinite loops, or the loop body may never execute, resulting in program errors or performance issues. Ensuring that the loop condition is dynamic or valid can reduce potential logical errors.

##### Error Example
'''php
while (false) {
    echo "This code will never be executed";
}

while (1 === 1) {
    // This code will cause an infinite loop
}
'''\n
##### Correct Example
'''php
$condition = true;
while ($condition) {
    echo "This code will execute when the condition is true";
    // Update the condition to avoid infinite loops
    $condition = false;
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则检测在 `while` 循环中条件始终为 `true` 的情况。

##### 规则意义
无限循环可能导致程序挂起，影响系统性能和用户体验。因此，确保 `while` 循环条件的合理性对于维护代码质量至关重要。

##### 错误示例
```php
while (true) {
    // 整个循环将永远执行，程序将进入无限循环。
}
```

##### 正确示例
```php
$counter = 0;
while ($counter < 10) {
    // 循环条件可以正常终止
    $counter++;
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule detects situations where the condition in a `while` loop is always `true`.

##### Rule Significance
Infinite loops can lead to program hangs, affecting system performance and user experience. Therefore, ensuring the rationality of `while` loop conditions is crucial for maintaining code quality.

##### Error Example
```php
while (true) {
    // The entire loop will execute forever, causing the program to enter an infinite loop.
}
```

##### Correct Example
```php
$counter = 0;
while ($counter < 10) {
    // The loop condition can terminate normally
    $counter++;
}
```
